{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPyPvjJXVLvR5BhnXByivD","type":"tool_result","content":"./.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/06-llm-protocols.md\n.scratch:\nts-rewrite/\n\ndocs:\nadr/\nagents/\nsecurity-model.md\nsuperpowers/\nc04e9f0 redeye: update ticket checklists\nc3d906c redeye: 10-review-scope.md done (respawn)\ndee748f Merge branch 'wip' into roast--ts-rewrite-10-review-scope\n// Version, commit, and build date. The bundle step injects them through\n// esbuild defines; a build without them (the test bundle, running from\n// source) gets the sentinels dev, unknown, unknown.\n\nexport interface BuildInfo {\n    version:string;\n    commit:string;\n    date:string;\n}\n\nexport const buildInfo:BuildInfo = {\n    version:typeof __ROAST_VERSION__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_VERSION__ :\n        'dev',\n    commit:typeof __ROAST_COMMIT__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_COMMIT__ :\n        'unknown',\n    date:typeof __ROAST_DATE__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_DATE__ :\n        'unknown',\n}\n\n// The one-line build string (Go buildinfo.String).\nexport function formatBuildInfo (info:BuildInfo):string {\n    if (info.version === 'dev' || info.date === 'unknown') {\n        return `${info.version} (commit ${info.commit})`\n    }\n    return `${info.version} (${info.commit}, ${info.date})`\n}\n# Roast\n\nAn adversarial, cross-model code reviewer installed as a project dependency\nvia npm. One model proposes defects in a Git diff and a second model checks\neach one before it reaches the report.\n\n## Language\n\n### Review\n\n**Finder**:\nThe role whose model reads the diff and proposes candidate findings.\n_Avoid_: reviewer, author model\n\n**Verifier**:\nThe role whose model re-reads the cited code and confirms or refutes each\ncandidate finding.\n_Avoid_: checker, judge\n\n**Role**:\nOne of the two review positions, finder or verifier, each bound to one\ninference profile.\n\n**Inference profile**:\nA named, complete unit of model, endpoint, protocol, output limit and\ncredential source.\n_Avoid_: provider, backend\n\n**Run record**:\nThe stored evidence of one review, kept inside the project that was reviewed.\n_Avoid_: log, history\n\n**Gate**:\nThe pre-commit hook that runs a quick review of staged content and fails open.\n_Avoid_: pre-commit check, hook\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Project config**:\nThe `.roast.json` file (JSONC) nearest the working directory, searched upward\nno further than the Git toplevel. It is the single home for every non-secret\nsetting.\n_Avoid_: repo config, local config, rc file\n\n**Trusted project config**:\nA project config whose security-relevant contents (non-default endpoints,\ncredential variable names, prompt-override files) the user has explicitly\napproved for this clone. Roast does not send code or credentials anywhere a\nproject config names until it is trusted.\n_Avoid_: allowed config, whitelisted config","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e41e09b0-fa4c-45a2-9b40-31ad5830b305","uuid":"edc93def-f0f8-44e6-84ec-542056a9635f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:44:26.971Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"./.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/06-llm-protocols.md\n.scratch:\nts-rewrite/\n\ndocs:\nadr/\nagents/\nsecurity-model.md\nsuperpowers/\nc04e9f0 redeye: update ticket checklists\nc3d906c redeye: 10-review-scope.md done (respawn)\ndee748f Merge branch 'wip' into roast--ts-rewrite-10-review-scope\n// Version, commit, and build date. The bundle step injects them through\n// esbuild defines; a build without them (the test bundle, running from\n// source) gets the sentinels dev, unknown, unknown.\n\nexport interface BuildInfo {\n    version:string;\n    commit:string;\n    date:string;\n}\n\nexport const buildInfo:BuildInfo = {\n    version:typeof __ROAST_VERSION__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_VERSION__ :\n        'dev',\n    commit:typeof __ROAST_COMMIT__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_COMMIT__ :\n        'unknown',\n    date:typeof __ROAST_DATE__ === 'string' ?\n        __ROAST_DATE__ :\n        'unknown',\n}\n\n// The one-line build string (Go buildinfo.String).\nexport function formatBuildInfo (info:BuildInfo):string {\n    if (info.version === 'dev' || info.date === 'unknown') {\n        return `${info.version} (commit ${info.commit})`\n    }\n    return `${info.version} (${info.commit}, ${info.date})`\n}\n# Roast\n\nAn adversarial, cross-model code reviewer installed as a project dependency\nvia npm. One model proposes defects in a Git diff and a second model checks\neach one before it reaches the report.\n\n## Language\n\n### Review\n\n**Finder**:\nThe role whose model reads the diff and proposes candidate findings.\n_Avoid_: reviewer, author model\n\n**Verifier**:\nThe role whose model re-reads the cited code and confirms or refutes each\ncandidate finding.\n_Avoid_: checker, judge\n\n**Role**:\nOne of the two review positions, finder or verifier, each bound to one\ninference profile.\n\n**Inference profile**:\nA named, complete unit of model, endpoint, protocol, output limit and\ncredential source.\n_Avoid_: provider, backend\n\n**Run record**:\nThe stored evidence of one review, kept inside the project that was reviewed.\n_Avoid_: log, history\n\n**Gate**:\nThe pre-commit hook that runs a quick review of staged content and fails open.\n_Avoid_: pre-commit check, hook\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Project config**:\nThe `.roast.json` file (JSONC) nearest the working directory, searched upward\nno further than the Git toplevel. It is the single home for every non-secret\nsetting.\n_Avoid_: repo config, local config, rc file\n\n**Trusted project config**:\nA project config whose security-relevant contents (non-default endpoints,\ncredential variable names, prompt-override files) the user has explicitly\napproved for this clone. Roast does not send code or credentials anywhere a\nproject config names until it is trusted.\n_Avoid_: allowed config, whitelisted config","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isIm