{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyZgiNxVeiNnr574iCfrvk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 06 -- LLM protocol adapters\n2\t\n3\tArea: the three inference wire protocols (`chat`, `responses`,\n4\t`anthropic`; OpenRouter is reached through `chat` or `responses`) spoken\n5\tover raw `fetch`, the shared SSE parser, raw response capture, error\n6\tclassification, and usage normalization. The agent loop, token ledger,\n7\twrap-up turn, final-tool validation and the retry loop itself belong to the\n8\tagent-loop area; this file defines the adapter interface that area\n9\tconsumes and the error/usage values it receives.\n10\t\n11\t## 1. Purpose\n12\t\n13\tEach **role** (finder, verifier) is bound to one **inference profile**: a\n14\tmodel, an endpoint (base URL), a protocol, an output limit, an optional\n15\t`session_header`, and a **credential** resolved by the config area. This\n16\tarea turns one model turn of the agent loop (system prompt, conversation so\n17\tfar, tool set) into exactly one HTTP request in the profile's protocol,\n18\tstreams the response, and returns a protocol-neutral assistant turn: ordered\n19\ttext, reasoning and tool-call parts, a finish reason, and normalized token\n20\tusage.\n21\t\n22\tIt also enforces three security and evidence invariants that hold no\n23\tmatter which protocol is used:\n24\t\n25\t1. Only Roast's resolved configuration shapes a request. Nothing in the\n26\t   process environment adds a credential, header, base URL, or proxy\n27\t   setting through this layer.\n28\t2. A credential is never forwarded to a host the profile did not name:\n29\t   every redirect is refused (2.5).\n30\t3. Every successful (2xx) provider response body is captured, byte for\n31\t   byte and size-capped, into the **run record** before any tool call it\n32\t   contains can be dispatched; a capture failure is permanent.\n33\t\n34\t## 2. Behavior contract\n35\t\n36\t### 2.1 Client construction\n37\t\n38\tA client is created per role per run (and once per role by `doctor`) from:\n39\t\n40\t| field             | meaning                                             |\n41\t|-------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|\n42\t| `role`            | `\"finder\"`, `\"verifier\"`, or a doctor check name    |\n43\t| `baseUrl`         | profile endpoint; CLI trims trailing `/`            |\n44\t| `apiKey`          | resolved credential value                           |\n45\t| `model`           | model ID, sent verbatim as the body's `model`       |\n46\t| `protocol`        | `\"\"` or `\"chat\"`, `\"responses\"`, `\"anthropic\"`      |\n47\t| `maxOutputTokens` | positive integer                                    |\n48\t| `maxAttempts`     | attempts per model call; `<= 0` means 4             |\n49\t| `requestTimeout`  | per request; `0` disables                           |\n50\t| `sessionHeader`   | optional extra header name (validated by config)    |\n51\t| `captureResponse` | optional callback receiving each raw 2xx body       |\n52\t\n53\tConstruction is synchronous, performs no I/O, and fails with these\n54\tmessages (checked in this order):\n55\t\n56\t1. `maxOutputTokens <= 0` -> `<model>: max output tokens must be positive`\n57\t2. `apiKey.trim() === \"\"` -> `<model>: API key is not configured`\n58\t3. unknown protocol -> `unsupported inference protocol \"<protocol>\"`\n59\t\n60\tAn empty protocol is `chat` everywhere, including the `protocol` field of a\n61\tcaptured raw response (`protocolName`).\n62\t\n63\tBuilt-in endpoints (config area, restated for context): OpenAI\n64\t`https://api.openai.com/v1` (`responses`, `chat`), Anthropic\n65\t`https://api.anthropic.com/v1` (`anthropic`), OpenRouter\n66\t`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` (`chat`, `responses`). OpenRouter is never a\n67\tprotocol's implicit default endpoint.\n68\t\n69\t### 2.2 Endpoint URL\n70\t\n71\t`baseUrl` already has trailing slashes removed by the CLI; adapters remove\n72\tthem again defensively.\n73\t\n74\t| protocol    | request URL                                           |\n75\t|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n76\t| `chat`      | `<base>/chat/completions`                             |\n77\t| `responses` | `<base>/responses`                                    |\n78\t| `anthropic` | `<base'>/v1/messages`                                 |\n79\t\n80\tFor `anthropic`, `base'` is `base` with trailing `/` characters removed and\n81\tthen one trailing `/v1` removed if present. Roast profiles write Anthropic\n82\tendpoints with `/v1` like the OpenAI protocols, so\n83\t`https://api.anthropic.com/v1` -> `https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages`,\n84\tand `https://gw.example/anthropic` ->\n85\t`https://gw.example/anthropic/v1/messages`. OpenRouter chat therefore posts\n86\tto `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`.\n87\t\n88\tAll requests are `POST` with a JSON body.\n89\t\n90\t### 2.3 Request headers\n91\t\n92\tEvery request carries exactly these Roast-controlled headers:\n93\t\n94\t| header               | chat / responses        | anthropic             |\n95\t|----------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------|\n96\t| `Content-Type`       | `application/json`      | `application/json`    |\n97\t| credential           | `Authorization: Bearer <key>` | `X-Api-Key: <key>` |\n98\t| `Anthropic-Version`  | absent                  | `2023-06-01`          |\n99\t| `User-Agent`         | `roast/<version>`       | `roast/<version>`     |\n100\t| `X-Agent-Session-Id` | session ID              | session ID            |\n101\t| `<session_header>`   | session ID (if set)     | session ID (if set)   |\n102\t\n103\t- `<version>` is the package version (Go: `buildinfo.Version`, `dev` in\n104\t  tests). In TS it is injected at build time; tests may assert the prefix\n105\t  `roast/`.\n106\t- Anthropic requests never carry `Authorization`; chat/responses requests\n107\t  never carry `X-Api-Key`.\n108\t- Session ID: `roast-` followed by 26 characters of the RFC 4648 base32\n109\t  alphabet `A-Z2-7` from a CSPRNG (Go `crypto/rand.Text()`, 128 bits). The\n110\t  agent loop mints one per `converse` / `completeStructured` call and passes\n111\t  it in every request of that call, including retries and the wrap-up turn.\n112\t  Two concurrent conversations on one client have different IDs.\n113\t- The session headers are set last. Header names are case-insensitive, so\n114\t  a profile `session_header` of `x-opencode-session` yields one header with\n115\t  the session value. Config validation already rejects reserved names\n116\t  (`Authorization`, `X-Api-Key`, `Content-Type`, `User-Agent`,\n117\t  `X-Agent-Session-Id`, `Anthropic-Version`, `Anthropic-Beta`,\n118\t  `Anthropic-Workspace-Id`, `OpenAI-Organization`, `OpenAI-Project`, any\n119\t  `X-Stainless-*`, hop-by-hop and framing headers).\n120\t- `Accept` is not significant to any fake or provider Roast targets; the TS\n121\t  adapters send `Accept: text/event-stream`.\n122\t\n123\t### 2.4 Ambient environment never influences requests\n124\t\n125\tThe Go SDKs read `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`,\n126\t`OPENAI_ORG_ID`, `OPENAI_PROJECT_ID`, `OPENAI_CUSTOM_HEADERS`,\n127\t`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`,\n128\t`ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS`, `ANTHROPIC_PROFILE`, `ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID`,\n129\t`ANTHROPIC_CONFIG_DIR` profile files, and federation variables; Go Roast\n130\tstrips every header they could add (`sdkenv.go`). The TS adapters read no\n131\tenvironment variable at all, so the contract becomes structural:\n132\t\n133\t- Request URL, headers and body are a pure function of the client config,\n134\t  the session ID, and the model request.\n135\t- With any of the variables above set to junk (including a decoy base URL\n136\t  and custom headers naming `User-Agent` and `X-Agent-Session-Id`), the\n137\t  configured endpoint receives exactly one request per call, the credential\n138\t  header holds only the configured key, `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>`,\n139\t  there is one `X-Agent-Session-Id` starting `roast-`, no\n140\t  `OpenAI-Organization`, `OpenAI-Project`, `Anthropic-Workspace-Id` or\n141\t  custom header, no header value contains an ambient value, and the decoy\n142\t  receives nothing.\n143\t- Credential discovery from the environment happens only in the config\n144\t  area (`ROAST_<ROLE>_API_KEY`, `api_key_env`, provider variables, stored\n145\t  credentials). The adapter receives a finished key.\n146\t\n147\t### 2.5 Redirects\n148\t\n149\tEvery HTTP redirect is refused as an endpoint error, for all three\n150\tprotocols (deliberate change 8; Go followed redirects on `chat` and\n151\t`responses`). Every request uses `fetch(..., {redirect: 'manual'})` and any\n152\t3xx response is an endpoint failure: a non-2xx HTTP error (status 3xx, not\n153\tretryable, `ErrEndpoint`). The redirect target is never contacted, so it\n154\tnever sees `Authorization` or `X-Api-Key`.\n155\t\n156\t### 2.6 Request bodies\n157\t\n158\tCommon rules for all protocols:\n159\t\n160\t- `stream: true` always. Non-streaming generation is never used (Go's\n161\t  managed model returns `roast agent runtime requires streaming` for it).\n162\t- The model ID is sent verbatim.\n163\t- Tool choice is always automatic. Roast never forces a tool choice:\n164\t  thinking-mode providers (DeepSeek, Claude with thinking) reject forced\n165\t  choice with a 400. This holds for exploration turns, the wrap-up turn,\n166\t  and the single-call structured path.\n167\t- The tool set is identical on every request of one conversation, in the\n168\t  caller's order, including the wrap-up turn (it is part of the signed\n169\t  reasoning prefix). The agent loop decides the set; adapters serialize it.\n170\t- No temperature, top_p, penalties, seed, `user`, metadata, parallel tool\n171\t  flags (except Anthropic's below), prompt-cache keys, or cache-control\n172\t  markers are sent. Provider-side prompt caching is whatever the provider\n173\t  does automatically; Roast only reads cache counters back (2.9).\n174\t- No reasoning / thinking configuration is sent, with the one Anthropic\n175\t  exception in 2.6.3.\n176\t\n177\t#### 2.6.1 `chat` (OpenAI Chat Completions; OpenRouter, DeepSeek, others)\n178\t\n179\t```json\n180\t{\n181\t  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n182\t  \"messages\": [ ... ],\n183\t  \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n184\t  \"stream\": true,\n185\t  \"stream_options\": {\"include_usage\": true},\n186\t  \"tools\": [\n187\t    {\"type\": \"function\",\n188\t     \"function\": {\"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n189\t                  \"parameters\": { <complete caller JSON Schema> },\n190\t                  \"strict\": false}}\n191\t  ],\n192\t  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\"\n193\t}\n194\t```\n195\t\n196\t- Output limit field: `max_tokens`, except for models matched as reasoning\n197\t  models, which get `max_completion_tokens` instead (and no `max_tokens`).\n198\t  A model ID is a reasoning model when its lowercased ID matches\n199\t  `/(?:^|[-.])(?:o[134]|oss)|gpt-[5-9]|codex-|computer-use/` and does not\n200\t  match `/gpt-3|gpt-4|chatgpt-|-chat/`. This applies to every chat\n201\t  endpoint, including OpenRouter IDs such as `openai/gpt-5`.\n202\t- `tools` and `tool_choice` are omitted when the tool list is empty.\n203\t- `description` is always present (empty string when the tool has none).\n204\t- `parameters` is a deep copy of the caller's full schema, including\n205\t  `additionalProperties` and nested `required` arrays.\n206\t- Tool-call `arguments` are kept as the raw string received; the agent loop\n207\t  decodes them (2.8.4).\n208\t\n209\tMessage encoding (in conversation order):\n210\t\n211\t- system prompt: `{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n212\t- user text: `{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n213\t- assistant turn: see below\n214\t- tool result:\n215\t  `{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"<id>\",\"content\":\"<output>\"}`\n216\t\n217\tAssistant turn: one message\n218\t`{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"<texts joined by \\n>\",\"tool_calls\":[...],\n219\t\"reasoning_content\":\"<reasoning texts joined by \\n>\"}` where:\n220\t\n221\t- `content` is omitted when the turn has no text part.\n222\t- `tool_calls` entries are\n223\t  `{\"id\":\"<id>\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"<n>\",\n224\t  \"arguments\":\"<raw input string>\"}}`,\n225\t  in arrival order; omitted when none.\n226\t- `reasoning_content` is present whenever the turn has at least one\n227\t  reasoning part, even if the joined text is empty. DeepSeek thinking mode\n228\t  rejects a follow-up request with tools whose earlier assistant messages\n229\t  lack `reasoning_content`. OpenRouter's `reasoning` field is also replayed\n230\t  as `reasoning_content`.\n231\t- An assistant turn with neither text nor tool calls is dropped (even if it\n232\t  carried reasoning).\n233\t- Tool results carry the output string unchanged; an error result is the\n234\t  error text as plain content (no error flag exists on this protocol).\n235\t\n236\t#### 2.6.2 `responses` (OpenAI Responses API; OpenRouter)\n237\t\n238\t```json\n239\t{\n240\t  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n241\t  \"input\": [ ... ],\n242\t  \"max_output_tokens\": 4096,\n243\t  \"store\": false,\n244\t  \"stream\": true,\n245\t  \"tools\": [\n246\t    {\"type\": \"function\", \"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n247\t     \"parameters\": { <complete caller JSON Schema> }, \"strict\": false}\n248\t  ],\n249\t  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\"\n250\t}\n251\t```\n252\t\n253\t- `store` is always `false`; `previous_response_id` is never sent; the full\n254\t  conversation is replayed every request. No `include`, no `reasoning`.\n255\t- `tools` / `tool_choice` omitted when the tool list is empty.\n256\t\n257\tInput items:\n258\t\n259\t- system prompt: `{\"role\":\"<mode>\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}` (see below)\n260\t- user text:\n261\t  `{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}]}`\n262\t- assistant text: `{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n263\t- assistant tool call: `{\"type\":\"function_call\",\"call_id\":\"<id>\",\n264\t  \"name\":\"<n>\",\"arguments\":\"<raw>\"}`\n265\t- assistant reasoning: never replayed\n266\t- tool result:\n267\t  `{\"type\":\"function_call_output\",\"call_id\":\"<id>\",\"output\":\"<output>\"}`\n268\t\n269\tAssistant parts become separate items in arrival order. System message\n270\tmode: if the lowercased model ID matches `/gpt-3|gpt-4|chatgpt-|-chat/`,\n271\trole `system`; otherwise, if the model ID contains `o1-mini` or\n272\t`o1-preview`, the system prompt is dropped; otherwise role `developer`.\n273\t\n274\t#### 2.6.3 `anthropic` (native Messages API)\n275\t\n276\t```json\n277\t{\n278\t  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n279\t  \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n280\t  \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"<system prompt>\"}],\n281\t  \"messages\": [ ... ],\n282\t  \"stream\": true,\n283\t  \"tools\": [\n284\t    {\"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n285\t     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\",\n286\t                      \"properties\": { ... }, \"required\": [\"path\"]}}\n287\t  ],\n288\t  \"tool_choice\": {\"type\": \"auto\", \"disable_parallel_tool_use\": false}\n289\t}\n290\t```\n291\t\n292\t- `max_tokens` is the profile's `maxOutputTokens` exactly (a 32768 budget\n293\t  reaches the endpoint unchanged).\n294\t- `input_schema` is a deep copy of the caller's full JSON schema, including\n295\t  `additionalProperties` and nested `required` arrays (deliberate change\n296\t  21; Go dropped every top-level keyword except `type`, `properties` and\n297\t  `required` because of a Fantasy limitation). `type` is `\"object\"`;\n298\t  `required` is always present (`[]` when the schema has none).\n299\t- `tools` / `tool_choice` omitted when the tool list is empty.\n300\t- Thinking: no `thinking` field, except when the lowercased model ID\n301\t  contains `claude-mythos-preview`, which gets\n302\t  `\"thinking\": {\"type\": \"adaptive\", \"display\": \"summarized\"}` (kept for\n303\t  parity).\n304\t- No `cache_control` anywhere; no `anthropic-beta` header.\n305\t\n306\tMessage encoding: conversation items are grouped into alternating role\n307\tblocks. Consecutive user texts and tool results merge into one\n308\t`{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[...]}` message, blocks in order; consecutive\n309\tassistant turns merge into one assistant message.\n310\t\n311\t- user text: `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}`\n312\t- tool result: `{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"<id>\",\n313\t  \"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<output>\"}]}`, plus\n314\t  `\"is_error\":true` for error results\n315\t- assistant text: `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}`\n316\t- assistant thinking:\n317\t  `{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"<text>\",\"signature\":\"<sig>\"}`\n318\t- redacted thinking: `{\"type\":\"redacted_thinking\",\"data\":\"<data>\"}`\n319\t- assistant tool call:\n320\t  `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"<id>\",\"name\":\"<n>\",\"input\":<object>}`\n321\t\n322\t- Assistant blocks are replayed in exactly the order they arrived,\n323\t  including a thinking block that arrived after a tool call (it is signed\n324\t  over that call). Never reorder, merge, edit or drop a signed block: Claude\n325\t  5.1+ rejects a thinking block whose prefix (system prompt, tool set, and\n326\t  every earlier block) changed.\n327\t- A reasoning part with a signature replays as `thinking`; one with\n328\t  redacted data as `redacted_thinking`; one with neither is dropped.\n329\t- `tool_use.input` is the tool call's raw input parsed as a JSON object;\n330\t  blank input or input that does not parse to an object becomes `{}` (keeps\n331\t  the `tool_use` / `tool_result` pairing).\n332\t- An assistant message with no text and no tool use (thinking only) is\n333\t  dropped.\n334\t\n335\t### 2.7 SSE parsing (shared)\n336\t\n337\tOne parser for all protocols, consuming the response body as bytes:\n338\t\n339\t- UTF-8 decode incrementally; lines end in `\\n`, `\\r\\n` or `\\r`.\n340\t- Fields: `event:` sets the event name, `data:` appends a data line (joined\n341\t  with `\\n`), `id:` and `retry:` are ignored, lines starting `:` are\n342\t  comments (OpenRouter keepalives). One optional space after the colon is\n343\t  stripped. A blank line dispatches the event; an event with no data lines\n344\t  is skipped. A trailing event without a final blank line is dispatched at\n345\t  EOF.\n346\t- Parsing is lazy: bytes are read only as the protocol decoder asks for\n347\t  the next event. Decoders stop reading at their terminal event (below)\n348\t  without draining the rest of the body; the body is then cancelled.\n349\t\n350\tPer protocol event handling:\n351\t\n352\t- `chat`: the event name is ignored. Data `[DONE]` (prefix match) ends the\n353\t  stream. Data whose JSON has a top-level `error` member (any value) ends\n354\t  the stream with a stream error (2.10). Other data is a\n355\t  `chat.completion.chunk`.\n356\t- `responses`: the event name is ignored; dispatch on the data JSON's\n357\t  `type`.\n358\t- `anthropic`: events with an empty name or named `ping` are skipped; an\n359\t  event named `error` ends the stream with an error built from its data\n360\t  (`{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"...\",\"message\":\"...\"}}`). Others\n361\t  dispatch on the data JSON's `type`. Unknown types are ignored.\n362\t\n363\tMalformed JSON in a dispatched event fails the call with a non-retryable\n364\terror.\n365\t\n366\t### 2.8 Turn assembly\n367\t\n368\tThe adapter returns one `ModelTurn` per request (3.2): `parts` in arrival\n369\torder, `finishReason`, optional `rawFinishReason`, and `usage`. Finish\n370\treason categories (Fantasy's names, used verbatim in agent-loop messages):\n371\t`stop`, `length`, `content-filter`, `tool-calls`, `error`, `other`,\n372\t`unknown`.\n373\t\n374\t#### 2.8.1 `chat` chunks\n375\t\n376\tFor each chunk (single choice expected; all choices are processed):\n377\t\n378\t- `usage`: if the chunk's `usage.total_tokens` is a positive number, the\n379\t  turn's usage becomes this chunk's usage. A chunk without usage (or with\n380\t  non-positive `total_tokens`) leaves the last reported usage unchanged\n381\t  (deliberate change 14; Go reset it to empty).\n382\t- Reasoning: a delta whose `reasoning_content` (preferred) or `reasoning`\n383\t  field is a non-empty string appends to the open reasoning part (opening\n384\t  one if none). A delta with such a field present and non-null but empty\n385\t  also opens a reasoning part, unless the delta is a boundary or reasoning\n386\t  already ended. A boundary is a delta with non-empty `content`, any\n387\t  `tool_calls`, or a non-empty `finish_reason`; a boundary closes an open\n388\t  reasoning part (it stays in `parts`, possibly with empty text).\n389\t- `content`: appended to the open text part (opening one).\n390\t- `tool_calls[i]`: keyed by `index`. A new index whose `function.name` and\n391\t  `function.arguments` are both empty is ignored. Otherwise it opens a call\n392\t  with `id` (or `tool-call-<index>` when missing), `type` (default\n393\t  `function`; any other type fails the call), `name`, and initial\n394\t  arguments. Later deltas for a known index append `function.arguments`.\n395\t- `finish_reason`: the last non-empty value wins.\n396\t\n397\tAt end of stream (EOF or `[DONE]`):\n398\t\n399\t1. Map the raw finish: `stop` -> stop, `length` -> length,\n400\t   `content_filter` -> content-filter, `tool_calls` / `function_call` ->\n401\t   tool-calls, `insufficient_system_resource` (DeepSeek) -> error, anything\n402\t   else -> unknown.\n403\t2. If no finish reason arrived and there are tool calls: if any call's\n404\t   arguments are empty or not valid JSON, fail with the retryable\n405\t   incomplete-stream error; otherwise the finish is tool-calls.\n406\t3. If no finish reason arrived and there are no tool calls, fail with the\n407\t   incomplete-stream error.\n408\t4. Calls with empty arguments get `\"{}\"`.\n409\t5. If the mapped finish is length, error or content-filter and there are\n410\t   tool calls, the tool calls are suppressed (not in `parts`) and\n411\t   `rawFinishReason` is set.\n412\t6. Otherwise `rawFinishReason` is set when the mapped finish is length,\n413\t   content-filter, error or unknown (the agent loop prints\n414\t   `finish reason \"<category>\" (the provider sent \"<raw>\")` when they\n415\t   differ).\n416\t7. Tool-call parts are appended after text/reasoning, sorted by index.\n417\t\n418\t#### 2.8.2 `responses` events\n419\t\n420\t- `response.created`: ignored.\n421\t- `response.output_item.added` with item type `function_call`: open a\n422\t  call at `output_index`.\n423\t- `response.function_call_arguments.delta`: ignored for the result.\n424\t- `response.output_item.done` with item type `function_call`: if a call\n425\t  is open at `output_index`, close it and emit the tool call\n426\t  `{id: item.call_id, name: item.name, input: item.arguments}`.\n427\t- `response.output_text.delta`: append `delta` to the text part.\n428\t- `response.reasoning_summary_text.delta`: append to a reasoning part\n429\t  (kept in `parts`, never replayed).\n430\t- `response.completed`, `response.incomplete`: terminal; finish and usage\n431\t  come from the event's `response`.\n432\t- `response.failed`: fail with\n433\t  `response failed: <response.error.message> (code: <code>)` (the code\n434\t  suffix only when non-empty); not retryable.\n435\t- `error`: fail with `response error: <message> (code: <code>)`; not\n436\t  retryable.\n437\t- anything else: ignored.\n438\t\n439\tFinish from `response.incomplete_details.reason` (`hasCall` = any tool call\n440\temitted):\n441\t\n442\t- `\"\"` or absent -> tool-calls if `hasCall`, else stop.\n443\t- `max_tokens`, `max_output_tokens` -> length.\n444\t- `content_filter` -> content-filter.\n445\t- anything else -> tool-calls if `hasCall`, else other.\n446\t\n447\t`response.status` is not consulted. Tool calls are kept even on length or\n448\tcontent-filter (the agent loop never dispatches them, 3.3). Ending without\n449\t`response.completed` or `response.incomplete` is the incomplete-stream\n450\terror.\n451\t\n452\t#### 2.8.3 `anthropic` events\n453\t\n454\t- `message_start`: usage := `message.usage`.\n455\t- `content_block_start`: open a block at `index`: `text`, `thinking`,\n456\t  `redacted_thinking` (its `data` comes from the start block), or\n457\t  `tool_use` (`id`, `name`).\n458\t- `content_block_delta`: `text_delta` appends to text;\n459\t  `thinking_delta` appends to thinking text; `signature_delta` appends to\n460\t  the signature; `input_json_delta` appends `partial_json`.\n461\t- `content_block_stop`: close the block. A `tool_use` emits a tool call\n462\t  whose input is the accumulated JSON, else the start block's `input`\n463\t  serialized when non-empty, else `\"{}\"`.\n464\t- `message_delta`: stop reason := `delta.stop_reason`;\n465\t  `usage.output_tokens` replaces output; `input_tokens`,\n466\t  `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens` replace the\n467\t  current values only when present and non-null.\n468\t- `message_stop`: terminal.\n469\t- anything else: ignored.\n470\t\n471\tParts are recorded in block-close order, which is index order for the\n472\tnative API. A thinking part keeps its text and signature; a\n473\t`redacted_thinking` part keeps `data`.\n474\t\n475\tFinish mapping: `end_turn`, `pause_turn`, `stop_sequence` -> stop;\n476\t`max_tokens`, `model_context_window_exceeded` -> length; `tool_use` ->\n477\ttool-calls; `refusal`, `content_filtered`, `guardrail_intervened` ->\n478\tcontent-filter; anything else -> unknown. If the stream ends without\n479\t`message_stop`, or with an empty stop reason, the call fails with the\n480\tretryable incomplete-stream error (pinned: a stream with complete tool\n481\tinput and `stop_reason` but no `message_stop` is retried and its partial\n482\ttool call never runs).\n483\t\n484\t#### 2.8.4 Decoding model output\n485\t\n486\tAll text decoded from provider bytes (text, reasoning, tool-call argument\n487\tstrings) replaces lone UTF-16 surrogates with U+FFFD at decode time\n488\t(cross-cutting \"Bytes and text\"). Tool arguments are decoded by the agent\n489\tloop with exact, case-sensitive key matching (deliberate change 7); a JSON\n490\t`null` argument means absent. Adapters pass the raw argument string through\n491\tand never repair or re-key it.\n492\t### 2.9 Usage normalization\n493\t\n494\t`Usage` (JSON names are used in run records):\n495\t\n496\t```ts\n497\tinterface Usage {\n498\t    uncachedInputTokens:number  // uncached_input_tokens\n499\t    cachedInputTokens:number    // cached_input_tokens\n500\t    cacheWriteTokens:number     // cache_write_tokens\n501\t    outputTokens:number         // output_tokens\n502\t    calls:number                // calls\n503\t}\n504\t```\n505\t\n506\tA client accumulates usage across all its calls (thread-safe in Go; in TS\n507\ta plain object mutated synchronously). A call contributes when the provider\n508\tdelivered its terminal finish (any finish reason, including abnormal ones),\n509\teven if the call then fails on capture or on a signal that fired at the\n510\tsame time (Go adds usage whenever a finish part was seen). A call that\n511\tfailed before a finish (HTTP error, stream error, incomplete stream,\n512\ttransport error, abort) contributes nothing and does not increment\n513\t`calls`. Each contributing call adds `calls: 1`. The same per-call value\n514\tis reported to the agent loop for the ledger release (3.2 `onUsage`).\n515\t\n516\tPer-response normalization subtracts cached tokens exactly once (deliberate\n517\tchange 13; Go subtracted them twice for `chat` and `responses`):\n518\t\n519\tStage 1, provider fields -> intermediate `{input, cacheRead, cacheWrite,\n520\toutput}`:\n521\t\n522\t- `chat`: `P = usage.prompt_tokens`, `C =\n523\t  usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, `O =\n524\t  usage.completion_tokens`, `R =\n525\t  usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens` (missing -> 0).\n526\t  `input = max(P - C, 0)`, `cacheRead = C`, `cacheWrite = 0`,\n527\t  `output = R > O ? O + R : O`.\n528\t- `responses`: same with `input_tokens`,\n529\t  `input_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, `output_tokens`,\n530\t  `output_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`.\n531\t- `anthropic`: `input = input_tokens`, `cacheRead =\n532\t  cache_read_input_tokens`, `cacheWrite = cache_creation_input_tokens`,\n533\t  `output = output_tokens` (after the accumulation in 2.8.3).\n534\t\n535\tStage 2, intermediate -> `Usage` (every value first clamped to `>= 0`),\n536\tthe same for every protocol because stage 1 already yields disjoint counts:\n537\t`uncached = input`, `cached = cacheRead`, `write = cacheWrite`,\n538\t`output = output`. There is no further subtraction. For `chat` and\n539\t`responses`, `prompt_tokens: 100, cached_tokens: 30` gives uncached 70 and\n540\tcached 30; `cached_tokens: 80` gives uncached 20 and cached 80.\n541\t\n542\tPinned values: two Anthropic responses each with `input_tokens: 10,\n543\toutput_tokens: 4, cache_creation_input_tokens: 2,\n544\tcache_read_input_tokens: 3` accumulate to `{uncached: 20, cached: 6,\n545\twrite: 4, output: 8, calls: 2}`. An intermediate of `{input: 8, cacheRead:\n546\t4, cacheWrite: 1, output: 3}` yields `{uncached: 8, cached: 4, write: 1,\n547\toutput: 3}` on every protocol.\n548\t\n549\tDeepSeek-specific counters (`prompt_cache_hit_tokens`,\n550\t`prompt_cache_miss_tokens`) are not read.\n551\t\n552\t### 2.10 Errors and classification\n553\t\n554\tEvery failure an adapter raises is one of:\n555\t\n556\t1. **HTTP error**: non-2xx status (3xx included, since redirects are not\n557\t   followed). The error body is read, at most 32 KiB (32768 bytes; the rest\n558\t   is discarded and the body cancelled; deliberate change 9), and is not\n559\t   captured. Fields: `status`, response headers (lowercased names),\n560\t   provider error `type`/`code` and `message` parsed best-effort from\n561\t   `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\"}}` or Anthropic's\n562\t   `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"message\"}}`. Retryable when any of:\n563\t   header `x-should-retry` is one of Go `ParseBool`'s true spellings (`1`,\n564\t   `t`, `T`, `true`, `TRUE`, `True`); status `408`, `409`, `429`, or\n565\t   `>= 500`. A false `x-should-retry` does not prevent a status-based\n566\t   retry.\n567\t   `401`, `403`, other 4xx, and 3xx are not retryable.\n568\t2. **Stream error**: an error delivered inside a 200 stream (chat `error`\n569\t   member, Anthropic `error` event). Retryable iff the provider error\n570\t   `type` (or `code` when type is empty) is one of `server_error`,\n571\t   `internal_error`, `overloaded_error`, `api_error`, `rate_limit_error`.\n572\t   Responses `response.failed` / `error` events are never retryable.\n573\t3. **Incomplete stream**: the body ended cleanly without the protocol's\n574\t   terminal signal (2.8). Message `stream transport error: unexpected EOF`.\n575\t   Retryable.\n576\t4. **Transport error**: `fetch` rejected or the body read failed for a\n577\t   network reason (connection refused/reset, DNS failure, socket closed,\n578\t   TLS failure, HTTP/2 stream reset, unexpected EOF mid-body). Retryable.\n579\t5. **Abort**: the request's `AbortSignal` fired (caller cancellation, the\n580\t   agent loop's work deadline, or the per-request timeout). Never retried.\n581\t   The adapter rethrows the signal's reason unchanged so the caller can tell\n582\t   them apart.\n583\t6. **Capture error** (2.11). Permanent; never retried, and it disables\n584\t   the client.\n585\t7. **Protocol error**: malformed event JSON, a non-`function` chat tool\n586\t   call type. Not retryable.\n587\t\n588\tRetry delay hints (consumed by the agent loop's retry policy, which owns\n589\tthe loop: up to `maxAttempts` attempts per model call, Go Fantasy\n590\t`DefaultRetryOptions` initial delay 5000 ms, factor 2, so 5 s, 10 s, 20 s):\n591\tfor an HTTP error with headers, `retry-after-ms` (float milliseconds), else\n592\t`retry-after` (float seconds, or an RFC 1123 date relative to now) gives\n593\t`hint`; the delay is `hint` when `hint > 0` and (`hint < 60 s` or `hint <\n594\tbackoff`), otherwise the exponential backoff. Adapters never retry\n595\tinternally (Go disables SDK retries: a 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches\n596\tthe server exactly once).\n597\t\n598\t`normalizeProviderError(outerSignal, model, err)` maps any error that\n599\tescapes the agent loop, in this order:\n600\t\n601\t1. `outerSignal.aborted` -> return `outerSignal.reason` (caller\n602\t   cancellation passes through untouched).\n603\t2. `err` is an abort or timeout (request timeout, work-deadline-bounded\n604\t   call) -> `ErrEndpoint` with message\n605\t   `llm: inference endpoint failure: <model>: <err message>`, keeping the\n606\t   timeout as `cause` (pinned: a request timeout is an endpoint failure that\n607\t   still identifies as a deadline).\n608\t3. `err` already is `ErrAuth`, `ErrEndpoint`, or `ErrBudgetExhausted`\n609\t   (ledger area) -> unchanged.\n610\t4. `err` carries HTTP status 401 or 403 anywhere in its cause chain ->\n611\t   `ErrAuth`: `llm: authentication failed: <err message>; check the\n612\t   configured API key`.\n613\t5. Otherwise -> `ErrEndpoint` as in step 2.\n614\t\n615\tSentinel kinds (Go `errors.go`) become error classes with a `kind` field\n616\tso callers test `err instanceof AuthError` or walk `cause`:\n617\t`ErrNoFinalCall` (`llm: tool loop ended without a final tool call`),\n618\t`ErrWorkDeadline` (`llm: work deadline reached`), `ErrAuth`\n619\t(`llm: authentication failed`), `ErrEndpoint`\n620\t(`llm: inference endpoint failure`). The first two are raised by the agent\n621\tloop; they are defined here so the whole `llm` error vocabulary lives in\n622\tone module.\n623\t\n624\t### 2.11 Raw response capture\n625\t\n626\tWhen `captureResponse` is configured, every 2xx response of every attempt\n627\tis captured as:\n628\t\n629\t```ts\n630\tinterface RawResponse {\n631\t    role:string         // client role\n632\t    protocol:string     // \"chat\" | \"responses\" | \"anthropic\"\n633\t    model:string\n634\t    contentType:'application/json'|'text/event-stream'\n635\t    body:Uint8Array     // exact bytes, no request, no headers\n636\t}\n637\t```\n638\t\n639\tRules (`maxCapturedResponseSize = 16 MiB = 16 << 20` bytes):\n640\t\n641\t1. Non-2xx responses are never captured. With no callback, nothing is\n642\t   captured or buffered.\n643\t2. If `Content-Length` exceeds 16 MiB, cancel the body and fail\n644\t   `capture <role> provider response: body exceeds 16777216-byte limit`.\n645\t3. Media type (parameters stripped, lowercased) `text/event-stream`:\n646\t   streaming capture. Do not read eagerly: the SSE parser pulls chunks,\n647\t   and each chunk is appended to the capture buffer as it is read. If a\n648\t   chunk would take the buffer over 16 MiB, fail with the size message;\n649\t   the callback is not called. When the adapter is done with the body\n650\t   (terminal event, error, abort, or EOF) it releases the body exactly\n651\t   once and then calls the callback with the bytes read so far, partial\n652\t   streams included (an interrupted stream's bytes are captured and the\n653\t   retry's stream is captured separately).\n654\t4. Any other media type: read the whole body with a 16 MiB + 1 limit,\n655\t   fail on overflow with the size message, fail if the bytes are not valid\n656\t   JSON with `capture <role> provider response: <model> returned invalid\n657\t   raw JSON`, else call the callback with `contentType:\n658\t   'application/json'`, then parse the bytes as SSE as usual (a JSON body\n659\t   yields no events and ends as an incomplete stream).\n660\t5. A callback failure fails with `capture <role> provider response:\n661\t   <callback error message>`.\n662\t6. Every capture failure is a `CaptureError`: permanent, never retried\n663\t   (pinned: one HTTP request with `maxAttempts: 3`), and sticky. After the\n664\t   first capture failure the client refuses every later request with the\n665\t   same error without contacting the server.\n666\t7. Ordering: the adapter resolves a turn only after the body has been\n667\t   released and the capture callback has succeeded, so no tool call from a\n668\t   response is dispatched before that response is in the run record. A\n669\t   capture failure discovered at release replaces any turn result.\n670\t8. Each in-flight request owns its own body and capture buffer; concurrent\n671\t   verifier calls on one client never share them.\n672\t\n673\t### 2.12 Request timeout and cancellation\n674\t\n675\t- The agent loop composes each request's signal from the caller's signal,\n676\t  the work-deadline bound (before the deadline fires) or the wrap-up window\n677\t  (after), and `AbortSignal.timeout(requestTimeout)` when\n678\t  `requestTimeout > 0` (CLI default 10 minutes; `doctor` uses 15 s).\n679\t- The timeout covers the whole request: connect, headers, and reading the\n680\t  full stream.\n681\t- An abort fails the call immediately (pinned: a 10 ms timeout returns\n682\t  within one second) and is never retried; the composed reason is rethrown\n683\t  (2.10 kind 5).\n684\t- After the stream loop the adapter re-checks the signal: a turn that\n685\t  completed while the signal fired is reported as the abort, not as a turn.\n686\t\n687\t### 2.13 Provider quirks (summary)\n688\t\n689\t- **DeepSeek** (chat and its Anthropic-compatible endpoint): thinking mode\n690\t  rejects any forced `tool_choice` (400 `Thinking mode does not support\n691\t  this tool_choice`), so choice is always `auto`; every earlier assistant\n692\t  message must replay `reasoning_content` (chat) or start with its\n693\t  `thinking` block (anthropic), which 2.6.1 and 2.6.3 guarantee;\n694\t  `insufficient_system_resource` maps to `error` and suppresses tool calls;\n695\t  a reasoning-only response with `length` finish is not retried (the agent\n696\t  loop reports it naming the model, `finish reason \"length\"`, and the\n697\t  `max_output_tokens` hint once).\n698\t- **OpenRouter**: `chat` at `/api/v1/chat/completions`; reasoning arrives as\n699\t  `reasoning` and is treated like `reasoning_content`; `:` comment lines\n700\t  are keepalives.\n701\t- **OpenAI reasoning models** on chat: `max_completion_tokens` (2.6.1).\n702\t- **Anthropic**: base URL `/v1` trimming, no redirects, `X-Api-Key` only,\n703\t  full `input_schema`, signed thinking replay.\n704\t- **Claude 5.1+ signed thinking**: blocks are bound to the system prompt,\n705\t  tool set and every earlier block; the adapter's job is byte-faithful\n706\t  replay of what it received (text, signature, order). Keeping the prefix\n707\t  stable across injected messages is the agent loop's job.\n708\t\n709\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n710\t\n711\tDirectory `src/llm/` (shared with the agent-loop area, which owns\n712\t`agent.ts`, `ledger.ts`, and the retry loop). Files owned by this area:\n713\t\n714\t| module                 | kind      | contents                             |\n715\t|------------------------|-----------|--------------------------------------|\n716\t| `types.ts`             | types     | protocol-neutral request/turn types  |\n717\t| `errors.ts`            | pure      | errors, retryability, delays     |\n718\t| `sse.ts`               | pure      | lazy SSE parser                      |\n719\t| `usage.ts`             | pure      | stage 1 + stage 2, accumulator   |\n720\t| `models.ts`            | pure      | model-ID rules (2.6)             |\n721\t| `chat.ts`              | pure      | chat request encoder and stream decoder |\n722\t| `responses.ts`         | pure      | responses encoder and decoder        |\n723\t| `anthropic.ts`         | pure      | anthropic encoder and decoder        |\n724\t| `capture.ts`           | shell     | body ownership, cap, sticky gate |\n725\t| `http.ts`              | shell     | swappable `fetch`, headers, redirects |\n726\t| `json.ts`              | pure      | tool-result JSON encoder, text decode |\n727\t| `session.ts`           | shell     | `newSessionId()`                     |\n728\t| `client.ts`            | shell     | `createModelClient`, `send`          |\n729\t\n730\tEncoders and decoders are pure: an encoder maps `(config, request)` to\n731\t`{url, headers, body}` without session or credential headers; a decoder\n732\tconsumes an `AsyncIterable<SseEvent>` and returns a `ModelTurn` or throws.\n733\tThis keeps every wire contract testable without sockets.\n734\t\n735\t### 3.1 Types (`types.ts`)\n736\t\n737\t```ts\n738\texport type Protocol = 'chat'|'responses'|'anthropic'\n739\t\n740\texport interface ClientConfig {\n741\t    role:string\n742\t    baseUrl:string\n743\t    apiKey:string\n744\t    model:string\n745\t    protocol:''|Protocol\n746\t    maxOutputTokens:number\n747\t    maxAttempts:number          // <= 0 -> 4 (DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS)\n748\t    requestTimeoutMs:number     // 0 disables\n749\t    sessionHeader?:string\n750\t    captureResponse?:(raw:RawResponse) => Promise<void>|void\n751\t}\n752\t\n753\texport interface ToolDefinition {\n754\t    name:string\n755\t    description:string\n756\t    schema:Record<string, unknown>   // complete caller JSON Schema\n757\t}\n758\t\n759\texport type AssistantPart =\n760\t    | { type:'text', text:string }\n761\t    | { type:'reasoning', text:string, signature?:string,\n762\t        redactedData?:string }\n763\t    | { type:'tool-call', id:string, name:string, input:string }\n764\t\n765\texport interface ToolResult {\n766\t    callId:string\n767\t    name:string\n768\t    output:string\n769\t    isError:boolean\n770\t}\n771\t\n772\texport type ConversationItem =\n773\t    | { role:'user', text:string }\n774\t    | { role:'assistant', parts:AssistantPart[] }\n775\t    | { role:'tool', results:ToolResult[] }\n776\t\n777\texport interface ModelRequest {\n778\t    system:string\n779\t    items:ConversationItem[]\n780\t    tools:ToolDefinition[]\n781\t    sessionId:string\n782\t    signal:AbortSignal            // already composed by the agent loop\n783\t    onUsage?:(usage:Usage) => void\n784\t}\n785\t\n786\texport type FinishReason =\n787\t    'stop'|'length'|'content-filter'|'tool-calls'|'error'|'other'|'unknown'\n788\t\n789\texport interface ModelTurn {\n790\t    parts:AssistantPart[]         // arrival order, replay verbatim\n791\t    finishReason:FinishReason\n792\t    rawFinishReason?:string\n793\t    usage:Usage                   // normalized, calls: 1\n794\t}\n795\t\n796\texport interface Usage {\n797\t    uncachedInputTokens:number\n798\t    cachedInputTokens:number\n799\t    cacheWriteTokens:number\n800\t    outputTokens:number\n801\t    calls:number\n802\t}\n803\t\n804\texport interface RawResponse {\n805\t    role:string\n806\t    protocol:Protocol\n807\t    model:string\n808\t    contentType:'application/json'|'text/event-stream'\n809\t    body:Uint8Array\n810\t}\n811\t```\n812\t\n813\tTool-call `input` is always the raw argument string as received (chat,\n814\tresponses) or as accumulated (anthropic). The agent loop parses and\n815\tvalidates it; adapters never repair JSON.\n816\t\n817\t### 3.2 Adapter interface consumed by the agent loop (`client.ts`)\n818\t\n819\t```ts\n820\texport interface ModelClient {\n821\t    readonly config:Readonly<ClientConfig>\n822\t    readonly protocol:Protocol           // '' normalized to 'chat'\n823\t    readonly maxAttempts:number          // normalized\n824\t    // One HTTP attempt. Never retries. Resolves only after capture\n825\t    // succeeded. Rejects with the kinds in 2.10.\n826\t    send(request:ModelRequest):Promise<ModelTurn>\n827\t    // Accumulated usage across all calls on this client.\n828\t    usage():Usage\n829\t}\n830\t\n831\texport function createModelClient(config:ClientConfig):ModelClient\n832\t```\n833\t\n834\t`send` steps:\n835\t\n836\t1. If the client's capture gate holds a failure, reject with it.\n837\t2. Encode with the protocol encoder; add credential, `User-Agent`,\n838\t   `Anthropic-Version` (anthropic), then `X-Agent-Session-Id` and\n839\t   `sessionHeader` set to `request.sessionId`.\n840\t3. `fetch` through `http.ts` with `request.signal` and `redirect:\n841\t   'manual'` for every protocol.\n842\t4. Non-2xx (including any 3xx): read at most 32 KiB of the error body,\n843\t   reject with an HTTP error (2.10).\n844\t5. 2xx: open the body through `capture.ts` (2.11), run the SSE parser\n845\t   lazily over it, and feed the protocol decoder.\n846\t6. When the decoder sees the terminal finish, compute usage, add it to the\n847\t   client total and call `request.onUsage` once.\n848\t7. Release the body (cancel the reader if not at EOF) and run the capture\n849\t   callback; a capture failure latches the gate and rejects.\n850\t8. If `request.signal.aborted`, reject with `signal.reason`.\n851\t9. Resolve the `ModelTurn`.\n852\t\n853\t### 3.3 Obligations the agent loop keeps (cross-reference)\n854\t\n855\tStated here so the boundary is unambiguous; specified in the agent-loop\n856\tarea:\n857\t\n858\t- Dispatch tool calls only from turns whose finish is `stop` or\n859\t  `tool-calls`; every other finish ends the attempt with a stop cause\n860\t  (`responses` may still return tool-call parts on length/content-filter).\n861\t- Mint one session ID per conversation; pass the same tool list on every\n862\t  turn; replay each `ModelTurn.parts` verbatim as an assistant item.\n863\t- Retry with `isRetryable(err)` and `retryDelayMs(err, backoffMs)` up to\n864\t  `maxAttempts`; never retry `CaptureError` or aborts.\n865\t- Compose the request signal (2.12) and map escaped errors with\n866\t  `normalizeProviderError`.\n867\t\n868\t### 3.4 Errors (`errors.ts`)\n869\t\n870\t```ts\n871\texport class LlmError extends Error { kind:string }\n872\texport class AuthError extends LlmError {}         // ErrAuth\n873\texport class EndpointError extends LlmError {}     // ErrEndpoint\n874\texport class NoFinalCallError extends LlmError {}  // agent loop\n875\texport class WorkDeadlineError extends LlmError {} // agent loop\n876\t\n877\texport class ProviderError extends Error {\n878\t    status?:number\n879\t    headers?:Record<string, string>   // lowercased names\n880\t    providerType?:string\n881\t    retryable:boolean\n882\t}\n883\texport class IncompleteStreamError extends ProviderError {}\n884\texport class CaptureError extends Error {}         // permanent\n885\t\n886\texport function isRetryable(err:unknown):boolean\n887\texport function retryDelayMs(err:unknown, backoffMs:number,\n888\t    now?:number):number\n889\texport function errorStatus(err:unknown):number|undefined // walks cause\n890\texport function normalizeProviderError(outer:AbortSignal, model:string,\n891\t    err:unknown):unknown\n892\t```\n893\t\n894\t`isRetryable`: false for aborts (`AbortError`, `TimeoutError`, or the\n895\tcomposed signal's reason) and `CaptureError`; `ProviderError.retryable`\n896\twhen present; true for transport errors (`TypeError` from `fetch` with a\n897\tnetwork `cause`, `UND_ERR_*` socket errors, `ECONNRESET`, `ECONNREFUSED`,\n898\t`ENOTFOUND`, `EAI_AGAIN`, `ETIMEDOUT`, `EPIPE`, premature close); false\n899\totherwise.\n900\t\n901\t### 3.5 Other modules\n902\t\n903\t- `sse.ts`: `parseSse(chunks:AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>):\n904\t  AsyncGenerator<{event:string, data:string}>`. Pull-based; never buffers\n905\t  more than the current chunk plus a partial line.\n906\t- `capture.ts`: `class CaptureGate { failure?:CaptureError }` per client;\n907\t  `openCapturedBody(response, config, gate):{chunks, release()}` where\n908\t  `release()` is idempotent, cancels the reader, then invokes the callback\n909\t  for SSE bodies. Non-SSE bodies are read, validated and captured inside\n910\t  `openCapturedBody` before `chunks` yields.\n911\t- `http.ts`: `let fetchImpl:typeof fetch = globalThis.fetch` plus\n912\t  `setFetch(f)` / `resetFetch()` for tests (the TS equivalent of Go's\n913\t  `redirectDefaultTransport`, shared with the login and doctor areas).\n914\t- `json.ts`: `encodeToolResult(value:unknown):string`, the one encoder for\n915\t  tool results sent to models (this area owns it; other areas import it).\n916\t  It sorts object keys (code-unit order, matching Go's map ordering) and\n917\t  does not HTML-escape `<`, `>`, `&` or U+2028/U+2029.\n918\t  `decodeModelText(bytes:Uint8Array):string` decodes UTF-8 and replaces\n919\t  lone surrogates with U+FFFD. Tool arguments the agent loop decodes match\n920\t  keys exactly (case-sensitive) and treat `null` as absent.\n921\t- `session.ts`: `newSessionId():string` using `crypto.getRandomValues`\n922\t  over 16 bytes encoded as unpadded base32 (26 characters) behind\n923\t  `roast-`.\n924\t- `models.ts`: `isChatReasoningModel(id)`, `responsesSystemMode(id):\n925\t  'system'|'developer'|'remove'`, `anthropicDefaultThinking(id)`.\n926\t\n927\tDependencies: none on other Roast areas except the version constant\n928\t(build-time define). The config area supplies `ClientConfig` values;\n929\tthe agent-loop and doctor areas consume `ModelClient`; the record area\n930\tsupplies `captureResponse`.\n931\t\n932\tDebug tracing (`roast:llm`): request URL host and path, protocol, model,\n933\tstatus, attempt outcome, finish reason, usage numbers, byte counts. Never\n934\tbodies, headers, prompts, keys, or session IDs' pairing with bodies.\n935\t\n936\t## 4. Deliberate changes\n937\t\n938\t- Raw `fetch` replaces Fantasy and the provider SDKs (settled decision).\n939\t  Consequences, none observable by Roast's contract: the incidental SDK\n940\t  headers (`X-Stainless-*`, `Idempotency-Key`, SDK `Accept`) are no longer\n941\t  sent; the ambient-environment stripping in Go's `sdkenv.go` becomes\n942\t  unnecessary because nothing reads the environment.\n943\t- Debug tracing via `@substrate-system/debug` namespace `roast:llm`, with\n944\t  no bodies, headers, prompts or credentials.\n945\t- Windows is unsupported (no effect on this area).\n946\t- spec.md deliberate changes applying here: 7 (exact JSON key match, `null`\n947\t  means absent), 8 (every redirect refused), 9 (error bodies capped at 32\n948\t  KiB), 13 (cached tokens subtracted once), 14 (chat usage kept across\n949\t  chunks without usage), 21 (Anthropic tools carry the full schema).\n950\t- No proxy library is bundled: the README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1`\n951\t  and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, and `doctor` warns when `HTTPS_PROXY` is set\n952\t  without `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY` (cross-cutting \"Network\"). Adapters still\n953\t  read no environment variable.\n954\t\n955\tNo other behavior changes; `claude-mythos-preview` keeps its default\n956\tadaptive thinking (parity).\n957\t\n958\t## 5. Test plan\n959\t\n960\tSeams: (C) CLI in-process `run(argv, io)` against a `node:http` fake\n961\tinference server, asserting requests received, exit codes, JSON output and\n962\trun-record files; (A) `createModelClient(...).send()` against a\n963\t`node:http` fake, used where the CLI cannot reach the behavior at\n964\treasonable cost (byte-level capture, concurrency, sticky failure); (U)\n965\tpure unit tests for the SSE parser, usage normalization and encoders.\n966\tA shared fixture writer ports `testutil.WriteInferenceStream`: from a\n967\tcomplete response object it emits the native SSE sequence for each\n968\tprotocol (chat chunks plus `[DONE]`; responses events with\n969\t`sequence_number`; anthropic `message_start` ... `message_stop`).\n970\t\n971\tWire shape and headers:\n972\t\n973\t- Anthropic posts to `<base>/v1/messages` after `/v1` trimming, sends\n974\t  `X-Api-Key`, a non-empty `Anthropic-Version`, `system`, `stream: true`,\n975\t  the same tools on the wrap-up turn, the full `input_schema` including\n976\t  `additionalProperties`, and the injected notice in the second request\n977\t  (`TestAnthropicAgentUsesNativeMessages`) (C).\n978\t- Anthropic `max_tokens` equals the profile budget for 1024 and 32768\n979\t  (`TestAnthropicNativeMessagesPreservesOutputBudget`) (C).\n980\t- Anthropic and structured calls use `tool_choice.type == \"auto\"`\n981\t  (`TestAnthropicCompleteStructuredUsesAutomaticToolChoice`) (C).\n982\t- Responses replays `function_call_output`, sends `store: false`, no\n983\t  `previous_response_id`, `tool_choice: \"auto\"`, identical tools on the\n984\t  final turn (`TestResponsesAgentReplaysToolOutputAndKeepsToolsOnFinalTurn`)\n985\t  (C).\n986\t- Tool schemas reach each protocol with `additionalProperties` and nested\n987\t  `required` lists intact\n988\t  (`TestToolSchemasCarryRequiredFields`) (C).\n989\t- `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>` (`TestUserAgentIncludesBuildVersion`)\n990\t  (U on the header builder).\n991\t- Chat `max_completion_tokens` for reasoning-model IDs, `max_tokens`\n992\t  otherwise; responses system mode by model (no Go test; new) (U).\n993\t\n994\tAmbient environment and credentials:\n995\t\n996\t- For each protocol and each env scenario (provider keys, auth token,\n997\t  explicit and fallback Anthropic profile, federation, custom headers),\n998\t  only the configured endpoint is called, once, with only Roast headers\n999\t  (`TestProvidersIgnoreAmbientSDKEnvironment`) (C).\n1000\t- Blank or whitespace key fails construction\n1001\t  (`TestNewRejectsMissingAPIKey`) (A).\n1002\t- Anthropic 401 maps to `AuthError`\n1003\t  (`TestAnthropicMapsAuthenticationFailure`) (C, exit code and JSON).\n1004\t- A 3xx from any protocol (`chat`, `responses`, `anthropic`) is not\n1005\t  followed, the target sees no key, and the error is an `EndpointError`,\n1006\t  not retried (`TestAnthropicDoesNotForwardCredentialsThroughRedirect`,\n1007\t  extended) (A).\n1008\t- An error body larger than 32 KiB is read only up to 32768 bytes (new)\n1009\t  (A).\n1010\t\n1011\tSession identity:\n1012\t\n1013\t- Two concurrent conversations get distinct `roast-` IDs, stable across a\n1014\t  retry and two turns, mirrored into `session_header`\n1015\t  (`TestProviderConversationIdentity`,\n1016\t  `TestStructuredCorrectionsRetainConversationIdentity`) (A).\n1017\t- Session header set once each, never duplicated; with the environment\n1018\t  naming the header it still carries Roast's value\n1019\t  (`TestSessionTransportDoesNotMutateRequests`,\n1020\t  `TestSessionHeaderOverridesEnvironmentHeader`) (A).\n1021\t\n1022\tCapture:\n1023\t\n1024\t- Callback failure: one HTTP request despite `maxAttempts: 3`, error\n1025\t  names the callback error (`TestCaptureFailureDoesNotRetryProviderCall`)\n1026\t  (C via a run-record write failure, or A).\n1027\t- `Content-Length: 16777217` fails with the size error\n1028\t  (`TestCaptureRejectsOversizedProviderResponse`) (A).\n1029\t- Invalid JSON 2xx body fails once, not retried\n1030\t  (`TestCaptureDoesNotRetryInvalidJSONResponse`) (A).\n1031\t- Streaming capture does not read ahead, preserves exactly the bytes read,\n1032\t  releases the body once (`TestStreamCaptureDoesNotEagerlyReadAndPreserves\n1033\t  PartialBytes`) (A with a controlled `ReadableStream`).\n1034\t- No `Content-Length`: overflow fails, callback not called, buffer never\n1035\t  exceeds the cap (`TestStreamCaptureEnforcesLimitWithoutContentLength`)\n1036\t  (U on `capture.ts`).\n1037\t- Interrupted Anthropic stream (no `message_stop`) is retried, its partial\n1038\t  tool never runs, all three streams are captured, usage counts only\n1039\t  completed calls\n1040\t  (`TestAnthropicInterruptedStreamRetriesWithoutExecutingPartialTools`)\n1041\t  (C, run-record raw responses).\n1042\t\n1043\tRetries and errors:\n1044\t\n1045\t- A 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches the server once for chat and\n1046\t  responses (`TestChatRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`,\n1047\t  `TestResponsesRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`) (C).\n1048\t- Request timeout yields `EndpointError` caused by a timeout within one\n1049\t  second (`TestInferenceRequestTimeoutIsEndpointFailure`) (A).\n1050\t- Classification table: 408/409/429/5xx/`x-should-retry` retryable,\n1051\t  401/403/3xx/400 not, transient stream types, incomplete stream,\n1052\t  transport errors, aborts (new) (U).\n1053\t- `retryDelayMs` with `retry-after-ms`, `retry-after` seconds and date,\n1054\t  out-of-range hints (new) (U).\n1055\t\n1056\tUsage:\n1057\t\n1058\t- Anthropic accumulation 20/6/4/8/2 (from\n1059\t  `TestAnthropicAgentUsesNativeMessages`) (C via `meta.json`).\n1060\t- Stage 2 on 8/4/1/3 -> 8/4/1/3 (`TestGenericUsageAccounting`, updated)\n1061\t  (U).\n1062\t- Chat and responses from fixture usage objects: `prompt_tokens: 100,\n1063\t  cached_tokens: 30` -> uncached 70, cached 30; cached 80 -> 20 and 80 (new)\n1064\t  (U).\n1065\t- A chat chunk without usage after a chunk with usage keeps the earlier\n1066\t  usage (new) (U).\n1067\t- `encodeToolResult` sorts keys and leaves `<>&` and U+2028 unescaped; a\n1068\t  lone surrogate in model output decodes to U+FFFD (new) (U).\n1069\t\n1070\tDeepSeek and finish reasons:\n1071\t\n1072\t- Forced tool choice never sent on chat or anthropic in any phase\n1073\t  (`TestDeepSeekThinkingModeUsesAutomaticToolChoice`,\n1074\t  `TestDeepSeekFixtureRejectsForcedToolChoice`) (C with a port of\n1075\t  `deepSeekThinkingServer`, which also rejects missing\n1076\t  `reasoning_content` / leading `thinking` replay).\n1077\t- Signed thinking prefix replay accepted by a binding fixture that rejects\n1078\t  any changed prefix (`TestAnthropicReplayKeepsSignedThinkingPrefix`,\n1079\t  `TestBindingServerRejectsChangedPrefix`) (A or C with a port of\n1080\t  `bindingServer`).\n1081\t- `insufficient_system_resource` -> `error`, `content_filter` ->\n1082\t  `content-filter`, unknown -> `unknown`, each with the raw reason exposed\n1083\t  (`TestAbnormalFinishNamesTheProviderReason`) (C).\n1084\t- Reasoning-only `length` finish is one request\n1085\t  (`TestReasoningOnlyLengthFinishNamesTheCeiling`) (C).\n1086\t\n1087\tSSE parser (U, new): CRLF/CR/LF, multi-line data, comments, missing final\n1088\tblank line, chunk boundaries inside a line and inside a UTF-8 sequence,\n1089\tlaziness (no read beyond the requested event).\n1090\t\n1091\tLive tests (opt-in, never CI): `ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\n1092\t(`_BASE_URL`, `_MODELS`), `ROAST_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` (`_BASE_URL`,\n1093\t`_MODEL`, `_PROTOCOL`) two-turn reviews and the DeepSeek reasoning ceiling\n1094\t(`TestLiveAnthropicTwoTurnReview`, `TestLiveDeepSeekTwoTurnReview`,\n1095\t`TestLiveDeepSeekReasoningCeiling`).\n1096\t\n1097\t## 6. Go baseline references\n1098\t\n1099\tAt commit `cd08f10`:\n1100\t\n1101\t- `internal/llm/provider.go` (client construction, capture transport,\n1102\t  usage normalization, `normalizeProviderError`, `errorStatus`)\n1103\t- `internal/llm/sdkenv.go`, `internal/llm/errors.go`, `internal/llm/llm.go`\n1104\t  (`Usage`, `Client`)\n1105\t- `internal/llm/agent.go` (`managedModel.Stream`, `streamCall`, tool\n1106\t  schema restoration, auto tool choice, session context, retry wiring)\n1107\t- `internal/config/provider.go`, `internal/config/config.go`\n1108\t  (`DefaultBaseURL`, `validateSessionHeader`), `internal/cli/cli.go`\n1109\t  (`clientConfig`, request-timeout default), `internal/cli/doctor.go`\n1110\t  (`doctorRoundtripCheck`)\n1111\t- `internal/testutil/inference.go` (SSE fixture writer)\n1112\t- Tests: `internal/llm/provider_test.go`, `ambient_env_test.go`,\n1113\t  `anthropic_budget_test.go`, `deepseek_test.go`, `session_test.go`,\n1114\t  `stream_capture_test.go`, `stream_test.go`, `thinking_binding_test.go`,\n1115\t  `tool_schema_test.go`, `agent_test.go` (usage, timeout), `live_test.go`;\n1116\t  `internal/cli/init_test.go` (`providerServer` routes)\n1117\t- Fantasy `charm.land/fantasy@v0.48.0`: `retry.go`, `errors.go`,\n1118\t  `providers/openai/language_model.go`, `language_model_hooks.go`,\n1119\t  `responses_language_model.go`, `reasoning.go`,\n1120\t  `providers/openaicompat/language_model_hooks.go`, `provider_options.go`,\n1121\t  `providers/anthropic/anthropic.go`, `error.go`; openai-go\n1122\t  `packages/ssestream`; anthropic-sdk-go v1.84.0 `packages/ssestream`,\n1123\t  `messageutil.go` (`Accumulate`), `internal/requestconfig`.\n1124\t\n1125\t## 7. Resolved\n1126\t\n1127\t1. Cached tokens are subtracted once for `chat` and `responses` (spec.md\n1128\t   deliberate change 13); stage 2 no longer subtracts (2.9).\n1129\t2. Every HTTP redirect is refused as an endpoint error for all protocols\n1130\t   (spec.md deliberate change 8; `redirect: 'manual'`, 2.5).\n1131\t3. No proxy library is bundled; README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` and\n1132\t   `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`; doctor warns on `HTTPS_PROXY` without\n1133\t   `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY` (spec.md cross-cutting \"Network\").\n1134\t4. Anthropic tool definitions carry the full JSON schema, including\n1135\t   `additionalProperties` (spec.md deliberate change 21).\n1136\t5. A chat chunk without usage keeps the last reported usage (spec.md\n1137\t   deliberate change 14).\n1138\t6. Provider error bodies are read at most 32 KiB (spec.md deliberate change\n1139\t   9).\n1140\t7. `claude-mythos-preview` keeps default adaptive thinking (spec.md\n1141\t   \"Further Notes\", parity).\n1142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e41e09b0-fa4c-45a2-9b40-31ad5830b305","uuid":"ac4e3e38-4fb1-4c28-82b5-72b2b9f6dfef","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:44:29.425Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-13-llm-core-chat-adapter/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/06-llm-protocols.md","content":"# 06 -- LLM protocol adapters\n\nArea: the three inference wire protocols (`chat`, `responses`,\n`anthropic`; OpenRouter is reached through `chat` or `responses`) spoken\nover raw `fetch`, the shared SSE parser, raw response capture, error\nclassification, and usage normalization. The agent loop, token ledger,\nwrap-up turn, final-tool validation and the retry loop itself belong to the\nagent-loop area; this file defines the adapter interface that area\nconsumes and the error/usage values it receives.\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nEach **role** (finder, verifier) is bound to one **inference profile**: a\nmodel, an endpoint (base URL), a protocol, an output limit, an optional\n`session_header`, and a **credential** resolved by the config area. This\narea turns one model turn of the agent loop (system prompt, conversation so\nfar, tool set) into exactly one HTTP request in the profile's protocol,\nstreams the response, and returns a protocol-neutral assistant turn: ordered\ntext, reasoning and tool-call parts, a finish reason, and normalized token\nusage.\n\nIt also enforces three security and evidence invariants that hold no\nmatter which protocol is used:\n\n1. Only Roast's resolved configuration shapes a request. Nothing in the\n   process environment adds a credential, header, base URL, or proxy\n   setting through this layer.\n2. A credential is never forwarded to a host the profile did not name:\n   every redirect is refused (2.5).\n3. Every successful (2xx) provider response body is captured, byte for\n   byte and size-capped, into the **run record** before any tool call it\n   contains can be dispatched; a capture failure is permanent.\n\n## 2. Behavior contract\n\n### 2.1 Client construction\n\nA client is created per role per run (and once per role by `doctor`) from:\n\n| field             | meaning                                             |\n|-------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|\n| `role`            | `\"finder\"`, `\"verifier\"`, or a doctor check name    |\n| `baseUrl`         | profile endpoint; CLI trims trailing `/`            |\n| `apiKey`          | resolved credential value                           |\n| `model`           | model ID, sent verbatim as the body's `model`       |\n| `protocol`        | `\"\"` or `\"chat\"`, `\"responses\"`, `\"anthropic\"`      |\n| `maxOutputTokens` | positive integer                                    |\n| `maxAttempts`     | attempts per model call; `<= 0` means 4             |\n| `requestTimeout`  | per request; `0` disables                           |\n| `sessionHeader`   | optional extra header name (validated by config)    |\n| `captureResponse` | optional callback receiving each raw 2xx body       |\n\nConstruction is synchronous, performs no I/O, and fails with these\nmessages (checked in this order):\n\n1. `maxOutputTokens <= 0` -> `<model>: max output tokens must be positive`\n2. `apiKey.trim() === \"\"` -> `<model>: API key is not configured`\n3. unknown protocol -> `unsupported inference protocol \"<protocol>\"`\n\nAn empty protocol is `chat` everywhere, including the `protocol` field of a\ncaptured raw response (`protocolName`).\n\nBuilt-in endpoints (config area, restated for context): OpenAI\n`https://api.openai.com/v1` (`responses`, `chat`), Anthropic\n`https://api.anthropic.com/v1` (`anthropic`), OpenRouter\n`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` (`chat`, `responses`). OpenRouter is never a\nprotocol's implicit default endpoint.\n\n### 2.2 Endpoint URL\n\n`baseUrl` already has trailing slashes removed by the CLI; adapters remove\nthem again defensively.\n\n| protocol    | request URL                                           |\n|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| `chat`      | `<base>/chat/completions`                             |\n| `responses` | `<base>/responses`                                    |\n| `anthropic` | `<base'>/v1/messages`                                 |\n\nFor `anthropic`, `base'` is `base` with trailing `/` characters removed and\nthen one trailing `/v1` removed if present. Roast profiles write Anthropic\nendpoints with `/v1` like the OpenAI protocols, so\n`https://api.anthropic.com/v1` -> `https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages`,\nand `https://gw.example/anthropic` ->\n`https://gw.example/anthropic/v1/messages`. OpenRouter chat therefore posts\nto `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`.\n\nAll requests are `POST` with a JSON body.\n\n### 2.3 Request headers\n\nEvery request carries exactly these Roast-controlled headers:\n\n| header               | chat / responses        | anthropic             |\n|----------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------|\n| `Content-Type`       | `application/json`      | `application/json`    |\n| credential           | `Authorization: Bearer <key>` | `X-Api-Key: <key>` |\n| `Anthropic-Version`  | absent                  | `2023-06-01`          |\n| `User-Agent`         | `roast/<version>`       | `roast/<version>`     |\n| `X-Agent-Session-Id` | session ID              | session ID            |\n| `<session_header>`   | session ID (if set)     | session ID (if set)   |\n\n- `<version>` is the package version (Go: `buildinfo.Version`, `dev` in\n  tests). In TS it is injected at build time; tests may assert the prefix\n  `roast/`.\n- Anthropic requests never carry `Authorization`; chat/responses requests\n  never carry `X-Api-Key`.\n- Session ID: `roast-` followed by 26 characters of the RFC 4648 base32\n  alphabet `A-Z2-7` from a CSPRNG (Go `crypto/rand.Text()`, 128 bits). The\n  agent loop mints one per `converse` / `completeStructured` call and passes\n  it in every request of that call, including retries and the wrap-up turn.\n  Two concurrent conversations on one client have different IDs.\n- The session headers are set last. Header names are case-insensitive, so\n  a profile `session_header` of `x-opencode-session` yields one header with\n  the session value. Config validation already rejects reserved names\n  (`Authorization`, `X-Api-Key`, `Content-Type`, `User-Agent`,\n  `X-Agent-Session-Id`, `Anthropic-Version`, `Anthropic-Beta`,\n  `Anthropic-Workspace-Id`, `OpenAI-Organization`, `OpenAI-Project`, any\n  `X-Stainless-*`, hop-by-hop and framing headers).\n- `Accept` is not significant to any fake or provider Roast targets; the TS\n  adapters send `Accept: text/event-stream`.\n\n### 2.4 Ambient environment never influences requests\n\nThe Go SDKs read `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`,\n`OPENAI_ORG_ID`, `OPENAI_PROJECT_ID`, `OPENAI_CUSTOM_HEADERS`,\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`,\n`ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS`, `ANTHROPIC_PROFILE`, `ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID`,\n`ANTHROPIC_CONFIG_DIR` profile files, and federation variables; Go Roast\nstrips every header they could add (`sdkenv.go`). The TS adapters read no\nenvironment variable at all, so the contract becomes structural:\n\n- Request URL, headers and body are a pure function of the client config,\n  the session ID, and the model request.\n- With any of the variables above set to junk (including a decoy base URL\n  and custom headers naming `User-Agent` and `X-Agent-Session-Id`), the\n  configured endpoint receives exactly one request per call, the credential\n  header holds only the configured key, `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>`,\n  there is one `X-Agent-Session-Id` starting `roast-`, no\n  `OpenAI-Organization`, `OpenAI-Project`, `Anthropic-Workspace-Id` or\n  custom header, no header value contains an ambient value, and the decoy\n  receives nothing.\n- Credential discovery from the environment happens only in the config\n  area (`ROAST_<ROLE>_API_KEY`, `api_key_env`, provider variables, stored\n  credentials). The adapter receives a finished key.\n\n### 2.5 Redirects\n\nEvery HTTP redirect is refused as an endpoint error, for all three\nprotocols (deliberate change 8; Go followed redirects on `chat` and\n`responses`). Every request uses `fetch(..., {redirect: 'manual'})` and any\n3xx response is an endpoint failure: a non-2xx HTTP error (status 3xx, not\nretryable, `ErrEndpoint`). The redirect target is never contacted, so it\nnever sees `Authorization` or `X-Api-Key`.\n\n### 2.6 Request bodies\n\nCommon rules for all protocols:\n\n- `stream: true` always. Non-streaming generation is never used (Go's\n  managed model returns `roast agent runtime requires streaming` for it).\n- The model ID is sent verbatim.\n- Tool choice is always automatic. Roast never forces a tool choice:\n  thinking-mode providers (DeepSeek, Claude with thinking) reject forced\n  choice with a 400. This holds for exploration turns, the wrap-up turn,\n  and the single-call structured path.\n- The tool set is identical on every request of one conversation, in the\n  caller's order, including the wrap-up turn (it is part of the signed\n  reasoning prefix). The agent loop decides the set; adapters serialize it.\n- No temperature, top_p, penalties, seed, `user`, metadata, parallel tool\n  flags (except Anthropic's below), prompt-cache keys, or cache-control\n  markers are sent. Provider-side prompt caching is whatever the provider\n  does automatically; Roast only reads cache counters back (2.9).\n- No reasoning / thinking configuration is sent, with the one Anthropic\n  exception in 2.6.3.\n\n#### 2.6.1 `chat` (OpenAI Chat Completions; OpenRouter, DeepSeek, others)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n  \"messages\": [ ... ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n  \"stream\": true,\n  \"stream_options\": {\"include_usage\": true},\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"type\": \"function\",\n     \"function\": {\"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n                  \"parameters\": { <complete caller JSON Schema> },\n                  \"strict\": false}}\n  ],\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\"\n}\n```\n\n- Output limit field: `max_tokens`, except for models matched as reasoning\n  models, which get `max_completion_tokens` instead (and no `max_tokens`).\n  A model ID is a reasoning model when its lowercased ID matches\n  `/(?:^|[-.])(?:o[134]|oss)|gpt-[5-9]|codex-|computer-use/` and does not\n  match `/gpt-3|gpt-4|chatgpt-|-chat/`. This applies to every chat\n  endpoint, including OpenRouter IDs such as `openai/gpt-5`.\n- `tools` and `tool_choice` are omitted when the tool list is empty.\n- `description` is always present (empty string when the tool has none).\n- `parameters` is a deep copy of the caller's full schema, including\n  `additionalProperties` and nested `required` arrays.\n- Tool-call `arguments` are kept as the raw string received; the agent loop\n  decodes them (2.8.4).\n\nMessage encoding (in conversation order):\n\n- system prompt: `{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n- user text: `{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n- assistant turn: see below\n- tool result:\n  `{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"<id>\",\"content\":\"<output>\"}`\n\nAssistant turn: one message\n`{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"<texts joined by \\n>\",\"tool_calls\":[...],\n\"reasoning_content\":\"<reasoning texts joined by \\n>\"}` where:\n\n- `content` is omitted when the turn has no text part.\n- `tool_calls` entries are\n  `{\"id\":\"<id>\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"<n>\",\n  \"arguments\":\"<raw input string>\"}}`,\n  in arrival order; omitted when none.\n- `reasoning_content` is present whenever the turn has at least one\n  reasoning part, even if the joined text is empty. DeepSeek thinking mode\n  rejects a follow-up request with tools whose earlier assistant messages\n  lack `reasoning_content`. OpenRouter's `reasoning` field is also replayed\n  as `reasoning_content`.\n- An assistant turn with neither text nor tool calls is dropped (even if it\n  carried reasoning).\n- Tool results carry the output string unchanged; an error result is the\n  error text as plain content (no error flag exists on this protocol).\n\n#### 2.6.2 `responses` (OpenAI Responses API; OpenRouter)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n  \"input\": [ ... ],\n  \"max_output_tokens\": 4096,\n  \"store\": false,\n  \"stream\": true,\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"type\": \"function\", \"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n     \"parameters\": { <complete caller JSON Schema> }, \"strict\": false}\n  ],\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\"\n}\n```\n\n- `store` is always `false`; `previous_response_id` is never sent; the full\n  conversation is replayed every request. No `include`, no `reasoning`.\n- `tools` / `tool_choice` omitted when the tool list is empty.\n\nInput items:\n\n- system prompt: `{\"role\":\"<mode>\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}` (see below)\n- user text:\n  `{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}]}`\n- assistant text: `{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"<text>\"}`\n- assistant tool call: `{\"type\":\"function_call\",\"call_id\":\"<id>\",\n  \"name\":\"<n>\",\"arguments\":\"<raw>\"}`\n- assistant reasoning: never replayed\n- tool result:\n  `{\"type\":\"function_call_output\",\"call_id\":\"<id>\",\"output\":\"<output>\"}`\n\nAssistant parts become separate items in arrival order. System message\nmode: if the lowercased model ID matches `/gpt-3|gpt-4|chatgpt-|-chat/`,\nrole `system`; otherwise, if the model ID contains `o1-mini` or\n`o1-preview`, the system prompt is dropped; otherwise role `developer`.\n\n#### 2.6.3 `anthropic` (native Messages API)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"<model>\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n  \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"<system prompt>\"}],\n  \"messages\": [ ... ],\n  \"stream\": true,\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"name\": \"read\", \"description\": \"...\",\n     \"input_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\",\n                      \"properties\": { ... }, \"required\": [\"path\"]}}\n  ],\n  \"tool_choice\": {\"type\": \"auto\", \"disable_parallel_tool_use\": false}\n}\n```\n\n- `max_tokens` is the profile's `maxOutputTokens` exactly (a 32768 budget\n  reaches the endpoint unchanged).\n- `input_schema` is a deep copy of the caller's full JSON schema, including\n  `additionalProperties` and nested `required` arrays (deliberate change\n  21; Go dropped every top-level keyword except `type`, `properties` and\n  `required` because of a Fantasy limitation). `type` is `\"object\"`;\n  `required` is always present (`[]` when the schema has none).\n- `tools` / `tool_choice` omitted when the tool list is empty.\n- Thinking: no `thinking` field, except when the lowercased model ID\n  contains `claude-mythos-preview`, which gets\n  `\"thinking\": {\"type\": \"adaptive\", \"display\": \"summarized\"}` (kept for\n  parity).\n- No `cache_control` anywhere; no `anthropic-beta` header.\n\nMessage encoding: conversation items are grouped into alternating role\nblocks. Consecutive user texts and tool results merge into one\n`{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[...]}` message, blocks in order; consecutive\nassistant turns merge into one assistant message.\n\n- user text: `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}`\n- tool result: `{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"<id>\",\n  \"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<output>\"}]}`, plus\n  `\"is_error\":true` for error results\n- assistant text: `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<text>\"}`\n- assistant thinking:\n  `{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"<text>\",\"signature\":\"<sig>\"}`\n- redacted thinking: `{\"type\":\"redacted_thinking\",\"data\":\"<data>\"}`\n- assistant tool call:\n  `{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"<id>\",\"name\":\"<n>\",\"input\":<object>}`\n\n- Assistant blocks are replayed in exactly the order they arrived,\n  including a thinking block that arrived after a tool call (it is signed\n  over that call). Never reorder, merge, edit or drop a signed block: Claude\n  5.1+ rejects a thinking block whose prefix (system prompt, tool set, and\n  every earlier block) changed.\n- A reasoning part with a signature replays as `thinking`; one with\n  redacted data as `redacted_thinking`; one with neither is dropped.\n- `tool_use.input` is the tool call's raw input parsed as a JSON object;\n  blank input or input that does not parse to an object becomes `{}` (keeps\n  the `tool_use` / `tool_result` pairing).\n- An assistant message with no text and no tool use (thinking only) is\n  dropped.\n\n### 2.7 SSE parsing (shared)\n\nOne parser for all protocols, consuming the response body as bytes:\n\n- UTF-8 decode incrementally; lines end in `\\n`, `\\r\\n` or `\\r`.\n- Fields: `event:` sets the event name, `data:` appends a data line (joined\n  with `\\n`), `id:` and `retry:` are ignored, lines starting `:` are\n  comments (OpenRouter keepalives). One optional space after the colon is\n  stripped. A blank line dispatches the event; an event with no data lines\n  is skipped. A trailing event without a final blank line is dispatched at\n  EOF.\n- Parsing is lazy: bytes are read only as the protocol decoder asks for\n  the next event. Decoders stop reading at their terminal event (below)\n  without draining the rest of the body; the body is then cancelled.\n\nPer protocol event handling:\n\n- `chat`: the event name is ignored. Data `[DONE]` (prefix match) ends the\n  stream. Data whose JSON has a top-level `error` member (any value) ends\n  the stream with a stream error (2.10). Other data is a\n  `chat.completion.chunk`.\n- `responses`: the event name is ignored; dispatch on the data JSON's\n  `type`.\n- `anthropic`: events with an empty name or named `ping` are skipped; an\n  event named `error` ends the stream with an error built from its data\n  (`{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"...\",\"message\":\"...\"}}`). Others\n  dispatch on the data JSON's `type`. Unknown types are ignored.\n\nMalformed JSON in a dispatched event fails the call with a non-retryable\nerror.\n\n### 2.8 Turn assembly\n\nThe adapter returns one `ModelTurn` per request (3.2): `parts` in arrival\norder, `finishReason`, optional `rawFinishReason`, and `usage`. Finish\nreason categories (Fantasy's names, used verbatim in agent-loop messages):\n`stop`, `length`, `content-filter`, `tool-calls`, `error`, `other`,\n`unknown`.\n\n#### 2.8.1 `chat` chunks\n\nFor each chunk (single choice expected; all choices are processed):\n\n- `usage`: if the chunk's `usage.total_tokens` is a positive number, the\n  turn's usage becomes this chunk's usage. A chunk without usage (or with\n  non-positive `total_tokens`) leaves the last reported usage unchanged\n  (deliberate change 14; Go reset it to empty).\n- Reasoning: a delta whose `reasoning_content` (preferred) or `reasoning`\n  field is a non-empty string appends to the open reasoning part (opening\n  one if none). A delta with such a field present and non-null but empty\n  also opens a reasoning part, unless the delta is a boundary or reasoning\n  already ended. A boundary is a delta with non-empty `content`, any\n  `tool_calls`, or a non-empty `finish_reason`; a boundary closes an open\n  reasoning part (it stays in `parts`, possibly with empty text).\n- `content`: appended to the open text part (opening one).\n- `tool_calls[i]`: keyed by `index`. A new index whose `function.name` and\n  `function.arguments` are both empty is ignored. Otherwise it opens a call\n  with `id` (or `tool-call-<index>` when missing), `type` (default\n  `function`; any other type fails the call), `name`, and initial\n  arguments. Later deltas for a known index append `function.arguments`.\n- `finish_reason`: the last non-empty value wins.\n\nAt end of stream (EOF or `[DONE]`):\n\n1. Map the raw finish: `stop` -> stop, `length` -> length,\n   `content_filter` -> content-filter, `tool_calls` / `function_call` ->\n   tool-calls, `insufficient_system_resource` (DeepSeek) -> error, anything\n   else -> unknown.\n2. If no finish reason arrived and there are tool calls: if any call's\n   arguments are empty or not valid JSON, fail with the retryable\n   incomplete-stream error; otherwise the finish is tool-calls.\n3. If no finish reason arrived and there are no tool calls, fail with the\n   incomplete-stream error.\n4. Calls with empty arguments get `\"{}\"`.\n5. If the mapped finish is length, error or content-filter and there are\n   tool calls, the tool calls are suppressed (not in `parts`) and\n   `rawFinishReason` is set.\n6. Otherwise `rawFinishReason` is set when the mapped finish is length,\n   content-filter, error or unknown (the agent loop prints\n   `finish reason \"<category>\" (the provider sent \"<raw>\")` when they\n   differ).\n7. Tool-call parts are appended after text/reasoning, sorted by index.\n\n#### 2.8.2 `responses` events\n\n- `response.created`: ignored.\n- `response.output_item.added` with item type `function_call`: open a\n  call at `output_index`.\n- `response.function_call_arguments.delta`: ignored for the result.\n- `response.output_item.done` with item type `function_call`: if a call\n  is open at `output_index`, close it and emit the tool call\n  `{id: item.call_id, name: item.name, input: item.arguments}`.\n- `response.output_text.delta`: append `delta` to the text part.\n- `response.reasoning_summary_text.delta`: append to a reasoning part\n  (kept in `parts`, never replayed).\n- `response.completed`, `response.incomplete`: terminal; finish and usage\n  come from the event's `response`.\n- `response.failed`: fail with\n  `response failed: <response.error.message> (code: <code>)` (the code\n  suffix only when non-empty); not retryable.\n- `error`: fail with `response error: <message> (code: <code>)`; not\n  retryable.\n- anything else: ignored.\n\nFinish from `response.incomplete_details.reason` (`hasCall` = any tool call\nemitted):\n\n- `\"\"` or absent -> tool-calls if `hasCall`, else stop.\n- `max_tokens`, `max_output_tokens` -> length.\n- `content_filter` -> content-filter.\n- anything else -> tool-calls if `hasCall`, else other.\n\n`response.status` is not consulted. Tool calls are kept even on length or\ncontent-filter (the agent loop never dispatches them, 3.3). Ending without\n`response.completed` or `response.incomplete` is the incomplete-stream\nerror.\n\n#### 2.8.3 `anthropic` events\n\n- `message_start`: usage := `message.usage`.\n- `content_block_start`: open a block at `index`: `text`, `thinking`,\n  `redacted_thinking` (its `data` comes from the start block), or\n  `tool_use` (`id`, `name`).\n- `content_block_delta`: `text_delta` appends to text;\n  `thinking_delta` appends to thinking text; `signature_delta` appends to\n  the signature; `input_json_delta` appends `partial_json`.\n- `content_block_stop`: close the block. A `tool_use` emits a tool call\n  whose input is the accumulated JSON, else the start block's `input`\n  serialized when non-empty, else `\"{}\"`.\n- `message_delta`: stop reason := `delta.stop_reason`;\n  `usage.output_tokens` replaces output; `input_tokens`,\n  `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens` replace the\n  current values only when present and non-null.\n- `message_stop`: terminal.\n- anything else: ignored.\n\nParts are recorded in block-close order, which is index order for the\nnative API. A thinking part keeps its text and signature; a\n`redacted_thinking` part keeps `data`.\n\nFinish mapping: `end_turn`, `pause_turn`, `stop_sequence` -> stop;\n`max_tokens`, `model_context_window_exceeded` -> length; `tool_use` ->\ntool-calls; `refusal`, `content_filtered`, `guardrail_intervened` ->\ncontent-filter; anything else -> unknown. If the stream ends without\n`message_stop`, or with an empty stop reason, the call fails with the\nretryable incomplete-stream error (pinned: a stream with complete tool\ninput and `stop_reason` but no `message_stop` is retried and its partial\ntool call never runs).\n\n#### 2.8.4 Decoding model output\n\nAll text decoded from provider bytes (text, reasoning, tool-call argument\nstrings) replaces lone UTF-16 surrogates with U+FFFD at decode time\n(cross-cutting \"Bytes and text\"). Tool arguments are decoded by the agent\nloop with exact, case-sensitive key matching (deliberate change 7); a JSON\n`null` argument means absent. Adapters pass the raw argument string through\nand never repair or re-key it.\n### 2.9 Usage normalization\n\n`Usage` (JSON names are used in run records):\n\n```ts\ninterface Usage {\n    uncachedInputTokens:number  // uncached_input_tokens\n    cachedInputTokens:number    // cached_input_tokens\n    cacheWriteTokens:number     // cache_write_tokens\n    outputTokens:number         // output_tokens\n    calls:number                // calls\n}\n```\n\nA client accumulates usage across all its calls (thread-safe in Go; in TS\na plain object mutated synchronously). A call contributes when the provider\ndelivered its terminal finish (any finish reason, including abnormal ones),\neven if the call then fails on capture or on a signal that fired at the\nsame time (Go adds usage whenever a finish part was seen). A call that\nfailed before a finish (HTTP error, stream error, incomplete stream,\ntransport error, abort) contributes nothing and does not increment\n`calls`. Each contributing call adds `calls: 1`. The same per-call value\nis reported to the agent loop for the ledger release (3.2 `onUsage`).\n\nPer-response normalization subtracts cached tokens exactly once (deliberate\nchange 13; Go subtracted them twice for `chat` and `responses`):\n\nStage 1, provider fields -> intermediate `{input, cacheRead, cacheWrite,\noutput}`:\n\n- `chat`: `P = usage.prompt_tokens`, `C =\n  usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, `O =\n  usage.completion_tokens`, `R =\n  usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens` (missing -> 0).\n  `input = max(P - C, 0)`, `cacheRead = C`, `cacheWrite = 0`,\n  `output = R > O ? O + R : O`.\n- `responses`: same with `input_tokens`,\n  `input_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, `output_tokens`,\n  `output_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`.\n- `anthropic`: `input = input_tokens`, `cacheRead =\n  cache_read_input_tokens`, `cacheWrite = cache_creation_input_tokens`,\n  `output = output_tokens` (after the accumulation in 2.8.3).\n\nStage 2, intermediate -> `Usage` (every value first clamped to `>= 0`),\nthe same for every protocol because stage 1 already yields disjoint counts:\n`uncached = input`, `cached = cacheRead`, `write = cacheWrite`,\n`output = output`. There is no further subtraction. For `chat` and\n`responses`, `prompt_tokens: 100, cached_tokens: 30` gives uncached 70 and\ncached 30; `cached_tokens: 80` gives uncached 20 and cached 80.\n\nPinned values: two Anthropic responses each with `input_tokens: 10,\noutput_tokens: 4, cache_creation_input_tokens: 2,\ncache_read_input_tokens: 3` accumulate to `{uncached: 20, cached: 6,\nwrite: 4, output: 8, calls: 2}`. An intermediate of `{input: 8, cacheRead:\n4, cacheWrite: 1, output: 3}` yields `{uncached: 8, cached: 4, write: 1,\noutput: 3}` on every protocol.\n\nDeepSeek-specific counters (`prompt_cache_hit_tokens`,\n`prompt_cache_miss_tokens`) are not read.\n\n### 2.10 Errors and classification\n\nEvery failure an adapter raises is one of:\n\n1. **HTTP error**: non-2xx status (3xx included, since redirects are not\n   followed). The error body is read, at most 32 KiB (32768 bytes; the rest\n   is discarded and the body cancelled; deliberate change 9), and is not\n   captured. Fields: `status`, response headers (lowercased names),\n   provider error `type`/`code` and `message` parsed best-effort from\n   `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\"}}` or Anthropic's\n   `{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"message\"}}`. Retryable when any of:\n   header `x-should-retry` is one of Go `ParseBool`'s true spellings (`1`,\n   `t`, `T`, `true`, `TRUE`, `True`); status `408`, `409`, `429`, or\n   `>= 500`. A false `x-should-retry` does not prevent a status-based\n   retry.\n   `401`, `403`, other 4xx, and 3xx are not retryable.\n2. **Stream error**: an error delivered inside a 200 stream (chat `error`\n   member, Anthropic `error` event). Retryable iff the provider error\n   `type` (or `code` when type is empty) is one of `server_error`,\n   `internal_error`, `overloaded_error`, `api_error`, `rate_limit_error`.\n   Responses `response.failed` / `error` events are never retryable.\n3. **Incomplete stream**: the body ended cleanly without the protocol's\n   terminal signal (2.8). Message `stream transport error: unexpected EOF`.\n   Retryable.\n4. **Transport error**: `fetch` rejected or the body read failed for a\n   network reason (connection refused/reset, DNS failure, socket closed,\n   TLS failure, HTTP/2 stream reset, unexpected EOF mid-body). Retryable.\n5. **Abort**: the request's `AbortSignal` fired (caller cancellation, the\n   agent loop's work deadline, or the per-request timeout). Never retried.\n   The adapter rethrows the signal's reason unchanged so the caller can tell\n   them apart.\n6. **Capture error** (2.11). Permanent; never retried, and it disables\n   the client.\n7. **Protocol error**: malformed event JSON, a non-`function` chat tool\n   call type. Not retryable.\n\nRetry delay hints (consumed by the agent loop's retry policy, which owns\nthe loop: up to `maxAttempts` attempts per model call, Go Fantasy\n`DefaultRetryOptions` initial delay 5000 ms, factor 2, so 5 s, 10 s, 20 s):\nfor an HTTP error with headers, `retry-after-ms` (float milliseconds), else\n`retry-after` (float seconds, or an RFC 1123 date relative to now) gives\n`hint`; the delay is `hint` when `hint > 0` and (`hint < 60 s` or `hint <\nbackoff`), otherwise the exponential backoff. Adapters never retry\ninternally (Go disables SDK retries: a 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches\nthe server exactly once).\n\n`normalizeProviderError(outerSignal, model, err)` maps any error that\nescapes the agent loop, in this order:\n\n1. `outerSignal.aborted` -> return `outerSignal.reason` (caller\n   cancellation passes through untouched).\n2. `err` is an abort or timeout (request timeout, work-deadline-bounded\n   call) -> `ErrEndpoint` with message\n   `llm: inference endpoint failure: <model>: <err message>`, keeping the\n   timeout as `cause` (pinned: a request timeout is an endpoint failure that\n   still identifies as a deadline).\n3. `err` already is `ErrAuth`, `ErrEndpoint`, or `ErrBudgetExhausted`\n   (ledger area) -> unchanged.\n4. `err` carries HTTP status 401 or 403 anywhere in its cause chain ->\n   `ErrAuth`: `llm: authentication failed: <err message>; check the\n   configured API key`.\n5. Otherwise -> `ErrEndpoint` as in step 2.\n\nSentinel kinds (Go `errors.go`) become error classes with a `kind` field\nso callers test `err instanceof AuthError` or walk `cause`:\n`ErrNoFinalCall` (`llm: tool loop ended without a final tool call`),\n`ErrWorkDeadline` (`llm: work deadline reached`), `ErrAuth`\n(`llm: authentication failed`), `ErrEndpoint`\n(`llm: inference endpoint failure`). The first two are raised by the agent\nloop; they are defined here so the whole `llm` error vocabulary lives in\none module.\n\n### 2.11 Raw response capture\n\nWhen `captureResponse` is configured, every 2xx response of every attempt\nis captured as:\n\n```ts\ninterface RawResponse {\n    role:string         // client role\n    protocol:string     // \"chat\" | \"responses\" | \"anthropic\"\n    model:string\n    contentType:'application/json'|'text/event-stream'\n    body:Uint8Array     // exact bytes, no request, no headers\n}\n```\n\nRules (`maxCapturedResponseSize = 16 MiB = 16 << 20` bytes):\n\n1. Non-2xx responses are never captured. With no callback, nothing is\n   captured or buffered.\n2. If `Content-Length` exceeds 16 MiB, cancel the body and fail\n   `capture <role> provider response: body exceeds 16777216-byte limit`.\n3. Media type (parameters stripped, lowercased) `text/event-stream`:\n   streaming capture. Do not read eagerly: the SSE parser pulls chunks,\n   and each chunk is appended to the capture buffer as it is read. If a\n   chunk would take the buffer over 16 MiB, fail with the size message;\n   the callback is not called. When the adapter is done with the body\n   (terminal event, error, abort, or EOF) it releases the body exactly\n   once and then calls the callback with the bytes read so far, partial\n   streams included (an interrupted stream's bytes are captured and the\n   retry's stream is captured separately).\n4. Any other media type: read the whole body with a 16 MiB + 1 limit,\n   fail on overflow with the size message, fail if the bytes are not valid\n   JSON with `capture <role> provider response: <model> returned invalid\n   raw JSON`, else call the callback with `contentType:\n   'application/json'`, then parse the bytes as SSE as usual (a JSON body\n   yields no events and ends as an incomplete stream).\n5. A callback failure fails with `capture <role> provider response:\n   <callback error message>`.\n6. Every capture failure is a `CaptureError`: permanent, never retried\n   (pinned: one HTTP request with `maxAttempts: 3`), and sticky. After the\n   first capture failure the client refuses every later request with the\n   same error without contacting the server.\n7. Ordering: the adapter resolves a turn only after the body has been\n   released and the capture callback has succeeded, so no tool call from a\n   response is dispatched before that response is in the run record. A\n   capture failure discovered at release replaces any turn result.\n8. Each in-flight request owns its own body and capture buffer; concurrent\n   verifier calls on one client never share them.\n\n### 2.12 Request timeout and cancellation\n\n- The agent loop composes each request's signal from the caller's signal,\n  the work-deadline bound (before the deadline fires) or the wrap-up window\n  (after), and `AbortSignal.timeout(requestTimeout)` when\n  `requestTimeout > 0` (CLI default 10 minutes; `doctor` uses 15 s).\n- The timeout covers the whole request: connect, headers, and reading the\n  full stream.\n- An abort fails the call immediately (pinned: a 10 ms timeout returns\n  within one second) and is never retried; the composed reason is rethrown\n  (2.10 kind 5).\n- After the stream loop the adapter re-checks the signal: a turn that\n  completed while the signal fired is reported as the abort, not as a turn.\n\n### 2.13 Provider quirks (summary)\n\n- **DeepSeek** (chat and its Anthropic-compatible endpoint): thinking mode\n  rejects any forced `tool_choice` (400 `Thinking mode does not support\n  this tool_choice`), so choice is always `auto`; every earlier assistant\n  message must replay `reasoning_content` (chat) or start with its\n  `thinking` block (anthropic), which 2.6.1 and 2.6.3 guarantee;\n  `insufficient_system_resource` maps to `error` and suppresses tool calls;\n  a reasoning-only response with `length` finish is not retried (the agent\n  loop reports it naming the model, `finish reason \"length\"`, and the\n  `max_output_tokens` hint once).\n- **OpenRouter**: `chat` at `/api/v1/chat/completions`; reasoning arrives as\n  `reasoning` and is treated like `reasoning_content`; `:` comment lines\n  are keepalives.\n- **OpenAI reasoning models** on chat: `max_completion_tokens` (2.6.1).\n- **Anthropic**: base URL `/v1` trimming, no redirects, `X-Api-Key` only,\n  full `input_schema`, signed thinking replay.\n- **Claude 5.1+ signed thinking**: blocks are bound to the system prompt,\n  tool set and every earlier block; the adapter's job is byte-faithful\n  replay of what it received (text, signature, order). Keeping the prefix\n  stable across injected messages is the agent loop's job.\n\n## 3. TypeScript module design\n\nDirectory `src/llm/` (shared with the agent-loop area, which owns\n`agent.ts`, `ledger.ts`, and the retry loop). Files owned by this area:\n\n| module                 | kind      | contents                             |\n|------------------------|-----------|--------------------------------------|\n| `types.ts`             | types     | protocol-neutral request/turn types  |\n| `errors.ts`            | pure      | errors, retryability, delays     |\n| `sse.ts`               | pure      | lazy SSE parser                      |\n| `usage.ts`             | pure      | stage 1 + stage 2, accumulator   |\n| `models.ts`            | pure      | model-ID rules (2.6)             |\n| `chat.ts`              | pure      | chat request encoder and stream decoder |\n| `responses.ts`         | pure      | responses encoder and decoder        |\n| `anthropic.ts`         | pure      | anthropic encoder and decoder        |\n| `capture.ts`           | shell     | body ownership, cap, sticky gate |\n| `http.ts`              | shell     | swappable `fetch`, headers, redirects |\n| `json.ts`              | pure      | tool-result JSON encoder, text decode |\n| `session.ts`           | shell     | `newSessionId()`                     |\n| `client.ts`            | shell     | `createModelClient`, `send`          |\n\nEncoders and decoders are pure: an encoder maps `(config, request)` to\n`{url, headers, body}` without session or credential headers; a decoder\nconsumes an `AsyncIterable<SseEvent>` and returns a `ModelTurn` or throws.\nThis keeps every wire contract testable without sockets.\n\n### 3.1 Types (`types.ts`)\n\n```ts\nexport type Protocol = 'chat'|'responses'|'anthropic'\n\nexport interface ClientConfig {\n    role:string\n    baseUrl:string\n    apiKey:string\n    model:string\n    protocol:''|Protocol\n    maxOutputTokens:number\n    maxAttempts:number          // <= 0 -> 4 (DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS)\n    requestTimeoutMs:number     // 0 disables\n    sessionHeader?:string\n    captureResponse?:(raw:RawResponse) => Promise<void>|void\n}\n\nexport interface ToolDefinition {\n    name:string\n    description:string\n    schema:Record<string, unknown>   // complete caller JSON Schema\n}\n\nexport type AssistantPart =\n    | { type:'text', text:string }\n    | { type:'reasoning', text:string, signature?:string,\n        redactedData?:string }\n    | { type:'tool-call', id:string, name:string, input:string }\n\nexport interface ToolResult {\n    callId:string\n    name:string\n    output:string\n    isError:boolean\n}\n\nexport type ConversationItem =\n    | { role:'user', text:string }\n    | { role:'assistant', parts:AssistantPart[] }\n    | { role:'tool', results:ToolResult[] }\n\nexport interface ModelRequest {\n    system:string\n    items:ConversationItem[]\n    tools:ToolDefinition[]\n    sessionId:string\n    signal:AbortSignal            // already composed by the agent loop\n    onUsage?:(usage:Usage) => void\n}\n\nexport type FinishReason =\n    'stop'|'length'|'content-filter'|'tool-calls'|'error'|'other'|'unknown'\n\nexport interface ModelTurn {\n    parts:AssistantPart[]         // arrival order, replay verbatim\n    finishReason:FinishReason\n    rawFinishReason?:string\n    usage:Usage                   // normalized, calls: 1\n}\n\nexport interface Usage {\n    uncachedInputTokens:number\n    cachedInputTokens:number\n    cacheWriteTokens:number\n    outputTokens:number\n    calls:number\n}\n\nexport interface RawResponse {\n    role:string\n    protocol:Protocol\n    model:string\n    contentType:'application/json'|'text/event-stream'\n    body:Uint8Array\n}\n```\n\nTool-call `input` is always the raw argument string as received (chat,\nresponses) or as accumulated (anthropic). The agent loop parses and\nvalidates it; adapters never repair JSON.\n\n### 3.2 Adapter interface consumed by the agent loop (`client.ts`)\n\n```ts\nexport interface ModelClient {\n    readonly config:Readonly<ClientConfig>\n    readonly protocol:Protocol           // '' normalized to 'chat'\n    readonly maxAttempts:number          // normalized\n    // One HTTP attempt. Never retries. Resolves only after capture\n    // succeeded. Rejects with the kinds in 2.10.\n    send(request:ModelRequest):Promise<ModelTurn>\n    // Accumulated usage across all calls on this client.\n    usage():Usage\n}\n\nexport function createModelClient(config:ClientConfig):ModelClient\n```\n\n`send` steps:\n\n1. If the client's capture gate holds a failure, reject with it.\n2. Encode with the protocol encoder; add credential, `User-Agent`,\n   `Anthropic-Version` (anthropic), then `X-Agent-Session-Id` and\n   `sessionHeader` set to `request.sessionId`.\n3. `fetch` through `http.ts` with `request.signal` and `redirect:\n   'manual'` for every protocol.\n4. Non-2xx (including any 3xx): read at most 32 KiB of the error body,\n   reject with an HTTP error (2.10).\n5. 2xx: open the body through `capture.ts` (2.11), run the SSE parser\n   lazily over it, and feed the protocol decoder.\n6. When the decoder sees the terminal finish, compute usage, add it to the\n   client total and call `request.onUsage` once.\n7. Release the body (cancel the reader if not at EOF) and run the capture\n   callback; a capture failure latches the gate and rejects.\n8. If `request.signal.aborted`, reject with `signal.reason`.\n9. Resolve the `ModelTurn`.\n\n### 3.3 Obligations the agent loop keeps (cross-reference)\n\nStated here so the boundary is unambiguous; specified in the agent-loop\narea:\n\n- Dispatch tool calls only from turns whose finish is `stop` or\n  `tool-calls`; every other finish ends the attempt with a stop cause\n  (`responses` may still return tool-call parts on length/content-filter).\n- Mint one session ID per conversation; pass the same tool list on every\n  turn; replay each `ModelTurn.parts` verbatim as an assistant item.\n- Retry with `isRetryable(err)` and `retryDelayMs(err, backoffMs)` up to\n  `maxAttempts`; never retry `CaptureError` or aborts.\n- Compose the request signal (2.12) and map escaped errors with\n  `normalizeProviderError`.\n\n### 3.4 Errors (`errors.ts`)\n\n```ts\nexport class LlmError extends Error { kind:string }\nexport class AuthError extends LlmError {}         // ErrAuth\nexport class EndpointError extends LlmError {}     // ErrEndpoint\nexport class NoFinalCallError extends LlmError {}  // agent loop\nexport class WorkDeadlineError extends LlmError {} // agent loop\n\nexport class ProviderError extends Error {\n    status?:number\n    headers?:Record<string, string>   // lowercased names\n    providerType?:string\n    retryable:boolean\n}\nexport class IncompleteStreamError extends ProviderError {}\nexport class CaptureError extends Error {}         // permanent\n\nexport function isRetryable(err:unknown):boolean\nexport function retryDelayMs(err:unknown, backoffMs:number,\n    now?:number):number\nexport function errorStatus(err:unknown):number|undefined // walks cause\nexport function normalizeProviderError(outer:AbortSignal, model:string,\n    err:unknown):unknown\n```\n\n`isRetryable`: false for aborts (`AbortError`, `TimeoutError`, or the\ncomposed signal's reason) and `CaptureError`; `ProviderError.retryable`\nwhen present; true for transport errors (`TypeError` from `fetch` with a\nnetwork `cause`, `UND_ERR_*` socket errors, `ECONNRESET`, `ECONNREFUSED`,\n`ENOTFOUND`, `EAI_AGAIN`, `ETIMEDOUT`, `EPIPE`, premature close); false\notherwise.\n\n### 3.5 Other modules\n\n- `sse.ts`: `parseSse(chunks:AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>):\n  AsyncGenerator<{event:string, data:string}>`. Pull-based; never buffers\n  more than the current chunk plus a partial line.\n- `capture.ts`: `class CaptureGate { failure?:CaptureError }` per client;\n  `openCapturedBody(response, config, gate):{chunks, release()}` where\n  `release()` is idempotent, cancels the reader, then invokes the callback\n  for SSE bodies. Non-SSE bodies are read, validated and captured inside\n  `openCapturedBody` before `chunks` yields.\n- `http.ts`: `let fetchImpl:typeof fetch = globalThis.fetch` plus\n  `setFetch(f)` / `resetFetch()` for tests (the TS equivalent of Go's\n  `redirectDefaultTransport`, shared with the login and doctor areas).\n- `json.ts`: `encodeToolResult(value:unknown):string`, the one encoder for\n  tool results sent to models (this area owns it; other areas import it).\n  It sorts object keys (code-unit order, matching Go's map ordering) and\n  does not HTML-escape `<`, `>`, `&` or U+2028/U+2029.\n  `decodeModelText(bytes:Uint8Array):string` decodes UTF-8 and replaces\n  lone surrogates with U+FFFD. Tool arguments the agent loop decodes match\n  keys exactly (case-sensitive) and treat `null` as absent.\n- `session.ts`: `newSessionId():string` using `crypto.getRandomValues`\n  over 16 bytes encoded as unpadded base32 (26 characters) behind\n  `roast-`.\n- `models.ts`: `isChatReasoningModel(id)`, `responsesSystemMode(id):\n  'system'|'developer'|'remove'`, `anthropicDefaultThinking(id)`.\n\nDependencies: none on other Roast areas except the version constant\n(build-time define). The config area supplies `ClientConfig` values;\nthe agent-loop and doctor areas consume `ModelClient`; the record area\nsupplies `captureResponse`.\n\nDebug tracing (`roast:llm`): request URL host and path, protocol, model,\nstatus, attempt outcome, finish reason, usage numbers, byte counts. Never\nbodies, headers, prompts, keys, or session IDs' pairing with bodies.\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n\n- Raw `fetch` replaces Fantasy and the provider SDKs (settled decision).\n  Consequences, none observable by Roast's contract: the incidental SDK\n  headers (`X-Stainless-*`, `Idempotency-Key`, SDK `Accept`) are no longer\n  sent; the ambient-environment stripping in Go's `sdkenv.go` becomes\n  unnecessary because nothing reads the environment.\n- Debug tracing via `@substrate-system/debug` namespace `roast:llm`, with\n  no bodies, headers, prompts or credentials.\n- Windows is unsupported (no effect on this area).\n- spec.md deliberate changes applying here: 7 (exact JSON key match, `null`\n  means absent), 8 (every redirect refused), 9 (error bodies capped at 32\n  KiB), 13 (cached tokens subtracted once), 14 (chat usage kept across\n  chunks without usage), 21 (Anthropic tools carry the full schema).\n- No proxy library is bundled: the README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1`\n  and `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, and `doctor` warns when `HTTPS_PROXY` is set\n  without `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY` (cross-cutting \"Network\"). Adapters still\n  read no environment variable.\n\nNo other behavior changes; `claude-mythos-preview` keeps its default\nadaptive thinking (parity).\n\n## 5. Test plan\n\nSeams: (C) CLI in-process `run(argv, io)` against a `node:http` fake\ninference server, asserting requests received, exit codes, JSON output and\nrun-record files; (A) `createModelClient(...).send()` against a\n`node:http` fake, used where the CLI cannot reach the behavior at\nreasonable cost (byte-level capture, concurrency, sticky failure); (U)\npure unit tests for the SSE parser, usage normalization and encoders.\nA shared fixture writer ports `testutil.WriteInferenceStream`: from a\ncomplete response object it emits the native SSE sequence for each\nprotocol (chat chunks plus `[DONE]`; responses events with\n`sequence_number`; anthropic `message_start` ... `message_stop`).\n\nWire shape and headers:\n\n- Anthropic posts to `<base>/v1/messages` after `/v1` trimming, sends\n  `X-Api-Key`, a non-empty `Anthropic-Version`, `system`, `stream: true`,\n  the same tools on the wrap-up turn, the full `input_schema` including\n  `additionalProperties`, and the injected notice in the second request\n  (`TestAnthropicAgentUsesNativeMessages`) (C).\n- Anthropic `max_tokens` equals the profile budget for 1024 and 32768\n  (`TestAnthropicNativeMessagesPreservesOutputBudget`) (C).\n- Anthropic and structured calls use `tool_choice.type == \"auto\"`\n  (`TestAnthropicCompleteStructuredUsesAutomaticToolChoice`) (C).\n- Responses replays `function_call_output`, sends `store: false`, no\n  `previous_response_id`, `tool_choice: \"auto\"`, identical tools on the\n  final turn (`TestResponsesAgentReplaysToolOutputAndKeepsToolsOnFinalTurn`)\n  (C).\n- Tool schemas reach each protocol with `additionalProperties` and nested\n  `required` lists intact\n  (`TestToolSchemasCarryRequiredFields`) (C).\n- `User-Agent` is `roast/<version>` (`TestUserAgentIncludesBuildVersion`)\n  (U on the header builder).\n- Chat `max_completion_tokens` for reasoning-model IDs, `max_tokens`\n  otherwise; responses system mode by model (no Go test; new) (U).\n\nAmbient environment and credentials:\n\n- For each protocol and each env scenario (provider keys, auth token,\n  explicit and fallback Anthropic profile, federation, custom headers),\n  only the configured endpoint is called, once, with only Roast headers\n  (`TestProvidersIgnoreAmbientSDKEnvironment`) (C).\n- Blank or whitespace key fails construction\n  (`TestNewRejectsMissingAPIKey`) (A).\n- Anthropic 401 maps to `AuthError`\n  (`TestAnthropicMapsAuthenticationFailure`) (C, exit code and JSON).\n- A 3xx from any protocol (`chat`, `responses`, `anthropic`) is not\n  followed, the target sees no key, and the error is an `EndpointError`,\n  not retried (`TestAnthropicDoesNotForwardCredentialsThroughRedirect`,\n  extended) (A).\n- An error body larger than 32 KiB is read only up to 32768 bytes (new)\n  (A).\n\nSession identity:\n\n- Two concurrent conversations get distinct `roast-` IDs, stable across a\n  retry and two turns, mirrored into `session_header`\n  (`TestProviderConversationIdentity`,\n  `TestStructuredCorrectionsRetainConversationIdentity`) (A).\n- Session header set once each, never duplicated; with the environment\n  naming the header it still carries Roast's value\n  (`TestSessionTransportDoesNotMutateRequests`,\n  `TestSessionHeaderOverridesEnvironmentHeader`) (A).\n\nCapture:\n\n- Callback failure: one HTTP request despite `maxAttempts: 3`, error\n  names the callback error (`TestCaptureFailureDoesNotRetryProviderCall`)\n  (C via a run-record write failure, or A).\n- `Content-Length: 16777217` fails with the size error\n  (`TestCaptureRejectsOversizedProviderResponse`) (A).\n- Invalid JSON 2xx body fails once, not retried\n  (`TestCaptureDoesNotRetryInvalidJSONResponse`) (A).\n- Streaming capture does not read ahead, preserves exactly the bytes read,\n  releases the body once (`TestStreamCaptureDoesNotEagerlyReadAndPreserves\n  PartialBytes`) (A with a controlled `ReadableStream`).\n- No `Content-Length`: overflow fails, callback not called, buffer never\n  exceeds the cap (`TestStreamCaptureEnforcesLimitWithoutContentLength`)\n  (U on `capture.ts`).\n- Interrupted Anthropic stream (no `message_stop`) is retried, its partial\n  tool never runs, all three streams are captured, usage counts only\n  completed calls\n  (`TestAnthropicInterruptedStreamRetriesWithoutExecutingPartialTools`)\n  (C, run-record raw responses).\n\nRetries and errors:\n\n- A 500 with `maxAttempts: 1` reaches the server once for chat and\n  responses (`TestChatRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`,\n  `TestResponsesRetriesOnlyThroughFantasy`) (C).\n- Request timeout yields `EndpointError` caused by a timeout within one\n  second (`TestInferenceRequestTimeoutIsEndpointFailure`) (A).\n- Classification table: 408/409/429/5xx/`x-should-retry` retryable,\n  401/403/3xx/400 not, transient stream types, incomplete stream,\n  transport errors, aborts (new) (U).\n- `retryDelayMs` with `retry-after-ms`, `retry-after` seconds and date,\n  out-of-range hints (new) (U).\n\nUsage:\n\n- Anthropic accumulation 20/6/4/8/2 (from\n  `TestAnthropicAgentUsesNativeMessages`) (C via `meta.json`).\n- Stage 2 on 8/4/1/3 -> 8/4/1/3 (`TestGenericUsageAccounting`, updated)\n  (U).\n- Chat and responses from fixture usage objects: `prompt_tokens: 100,\n  cached_tokens: 30` -> uncached 70, cached 30; cached 80 -> 20 and 80 (new)\n  (U).\n- A chat chunk without usage after a chunk with usage keeps the earlier\n  usage (new) (U).\n- `encodeToolResult` sorts keys and leaves `<>&` and U+2028 unescaped; a\n  lone surrogate in model output decodes to U+FFFD (new) (U).\n\nDeepSeek and finish reasons:\n\n- Forced tool choice never sent on chat or anthropic in any phase\n  (`TestDeepSeekThinkingModeUsesAutomaticToolChoice`,\n  `TestDeepSeekFixtureRejectsForcedToolChoice`) (C with a port of\n  `deepSeekThinkingServer`, which also rejects missing\n  `reasoning_content` / leading `thinking` replay).\n- Signed thinking prefix replay accepted by a binding fixture that rejects\n  any changed prefix (`TestAnthropicReplayKeepsSignedThinkingPrefix`,\n  `TestBindingServerRejectsChangedPrefix`) (A or C with a port of\n  `bindingServer`).\n- `insufficient_system_resource` -> `error`, `content_filter` ->\n  `content-filter`, unknown -> `unknown`, each with the raw reason exposed\n  (`TestAbnormalFinishNamesTheProviderReason`) (C).\n- Reasoning-only `length` finish is one request\n  (`TestReasoningOnlyLengthFinishNamesTheCeiling`) (C).\n\nSSE parser (U, new): CRLF/CR/LF, multi-line data, comments, missing final\nblank line, chunk boundaries inside a line and inside a UTF-8 sequence,\nlaziness (no read beyond the requested event).\n\nLive tests (opt-in, never CI): `ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\n(`_BASE_URL`, `_MODELS`), `ROAST_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` (`_BASE_URL`,\n`_MODEL`, `_PROTOCOL`) two-turn reviews and the DeepSeek reasoning ceiling\n(`TestLiveAnthropicTwoTurnReview`, `TestLiveDeepSeekTwoTurnReview`,\n`TestLiveDeepSeekReasoningCeiling`).\n\n## 6. Go baseline references\n\nAt commit `cd08f10`:\n\n- `internal/llm/provider.go` (client construction, capture transport,\n  usage normalization, `normalizeProviderError`, `errorStatus`)\n- `internal/llm/sdkenv.go`, `internal/llm/errors.go`, `internal/llm/llm.go`\n  (`Usage`, `Client`)\n- `internal/llm/agent.go` (`managedModel.Stream`, `streamCall`, tool\n  schema restoration, auto tool choice, session context, retry wiring)\n- `internal/config/provider.go`, `internal/config/config.go`\n  (`DefaultBaseURL`, `validateSessionHeader`), `internal/cli/cli.go`\n  (`clientConfig`, request-timeout default), `internal/cli/doctor.go`\n  (`doctorRoundtripCheck`)\n- `internal/testutil/inference.go` (SSE fixture writer)\n- Tests: `internal/llm/provider_test.go`, `ambient_env_test.go`,\n  `anthropic_budget_test.go`, `deepseek_test.go`, `session_test.go`,\n  `stream_capture_test.go`, `stream_test.go`, `thinking_binding_test.go`,\n  `tool_schema_test.go`, `agent_test.go` (usage, timeout), `live_test.go`;\n  `internal/cli/init_test.go` (`providerServer` routes)\n- Fantasy `charm.land/fantasy@v0.48.0`: `retry.go`, `errors.go`,\n  `providers/openai/language_model.go`, `language_model_hooks.go`,\n  `responses_language_model.go`, `reasoning.go`,\n  `providers/openaicompat/language_model_hooks.go`, `provider_options.go`,\n  `providers/anthropic/anthropic.go`, `error.go`; openai-go\n  `packages/ssestream`; anthropic-sdk-go v1.84.0 `packages/ssestream`,\n  `messageutil.go` (`Accumulate`), `internal/requestconfig`.\n\n## 7. Resolved\n\n1. Cached tokens are subtracted once for `chat` and `responses` (spec.md\n   deliberate change 13); stage 2 no longer subtracts (2.9).\n2. Every HTTP redirect is refused as an endpoint error for all protocols\n   (spec.md deliberate change 8; `redirect: 'manual'`, 2.5).\n3. No proxy library is bundled; README documents `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` and\n   `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`; doctor warns on `HTTPS_PROXY` without\n   `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY` (spec.md cross-cutting \"Network\").\n4. Anthropic tool definitions carry the full JSON schema, including\n   `additionalProperties` (spec.md deliberate change 21).\n5. A chat chunk without usage keeps the last reported usage (spec.md\n   deliberate change 14).\n6. Provider error bodies are read at most 32 KiB (spec.md deliberate change\n   9).\n7. `claude-mythos-preview` keeps default adaptive thinking (spec.md\n   \"Further Notes\", parity).\n","numLines":1142,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1142}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TyZgiNxVeiNnr574iCfrvk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
