rap-up: notice text and in-step switch\n404:### 2.10 Stop conditions, callbacks, and continuation\n443:### 2.11 Step retries\n469:### 2.12 Signed reasoning and conversation identity\n483:### 2.13 Token ledger\n566:### 2.14 Errors and result precedence\n632:### 2.15 Usage accounting\n651:## 3. TypeScript module design\n658:### 3.1 Adapter interface (assumed; owned by the LLM protocols area)\n702:### 3.2 Transcript (`src/llm/messages.ts`)\n726:### 3.3 Public types (`src/llm/types.ts`)\n787:### 3.4 Modules\n954:### 3.5 Dependencies\n970:## 4. Deliberate changes\n1001:## 5. Test plan\n1012:### 5.1 Finalization\n1056:### 5.2 Record tools and the deadline\n1083:### 5.3 Dispatch\n1099:### 5.4 Retries\n1107:### 5.5 Ledger and usage\n1129:### 5.6 Error naming and provider integration\n1156:## 6. Go baseline references\n1180:## 7. Resolved","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EzW5wq3fkFqoEBQrtoD1hS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
