{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016T7dEFKpRxrmV2dAkdnetQ","type":"tool_result","content":"### 3.7 Test fixtures\n\n- `test/helpers/env.ts`: `cleanEnv(base)` returns a copy of an env with\n  every variable whose upper-cased name starts with `ANTHROPIC_`,\n  `OPENAI_`, `OPENROUTER_`, or `ROAST_` removed. Tests build `io.env`\n  from it (plus `PATH`, `HOME` isolation, and explicit variables); no\n  test mutates `process.env`.\n- `test/helpers/inference-stream.ts`: `writeInferenceStream(res,\n  protocol, response)` turns a complete response object into the native\n  SSE stream for `anthropic`, `responses`, or `chat`, exactly as in\n  section 3.8. `writeJSONStream(res, protocol, body)` parses a JSON\n  string first. Unknown protocol -> error.\n- `test/helpers/run.ts`: `runRoast(args, opts)` wraps `run` with buffer\n  streams, a temp repo cwd, clean env, and an optional redirecting\n  `fetch`; returns `{code, error, stdout, stderr}`.\n- Terminal and browser swaps: `simulateTerminals(t, value)` and\n  `captureBrowser(t)` replace the module-level functions and restore\n  them at test end.\n\n### 3.8 SSE fixture format (`writeInferenceStream`)\n\nSets `Content-Type: text/event-stream`. Each event is\n`[event: <name>\\n]data: <json>\\n\\n`. For `responses`, every emitted\nobject gets `sequence_number` 0, 1, 2, ... in emission order.\n\n- `anthropic`: `message_start` with `message` = response with `content:\n  []`, `stop_reason: null`, `usage` copied with `output_tokens: 0`. For\n  each content block at index i: `content_block_start` (`index`,\n  `content_block` = block with `thinking` and `signature` emptied for\n  thinking, `text` emptied for text, `input: {}` for tool use); deltas\n  (`thinking_delta` + `signature_delta`; `text_delta`; or\n  `input_json_delta` with `partial_json` = JSON of the input);\n  `content_block_stop`. Then `message_delta` (`delta: {stop_reason,\n  stop_sequence: null}`, `usage` = response usage) and `message_stop`.\n  Event name = the object's `type`.\n- `responses`: `response.created` (`response` with `output: []`,\n  `status: in_progress`); per output item: `response.output_item.added`\n  (item with `arguments: \"\"`, `status: in_progress`),\n  `response.function_call_arguments.delta` (`item_id`, `delta` =\n  arguments), `response.function_call_arguments.done` (`arguments`),\n  `response.output_item.done` (full item), each with `output_index`;\n  then `response.completed` with the full response.\n- `chat`: no `event:` lines. Three chunks, each `{id, object:\n  \"chat.completion.chunk\", created: 1, model, choices}`: first, choices\n  with `delta` = message with `tool_calls` re-indexed (`index` = position)\n  and `finish_reason: null`; second, choices with empty `delta` and the\n  real `finish_reason`; third, `choices: []` plus `usage`. Then\n  `data: [DONE]\\n\\n`.\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n### 3.3 Public types (`src/llm/types.ts`)\n\n```ts\nexport interface Tool {\n    name:string\n    description:string\n    schema:JsonSchemaObject\n    // Absent for the final tool.\n    run?:(args:Record<string, unknown>, signal:AbortSignal) =>\n        unknown|Promise<unknown>\n    recordsResult?:boolean\n}\n\nexport interface TurnInfo {\n    turn:number\n    tool:string\n    args:Record<string, unknown>\n}\n\n// Type validation of the final arguments (2.7). `decode` receives the\n// value parsed with integer preservation and throws an Error whose\n// message is the validation detail.\nexport interface FinalSpec<T> {\n    decode(value:unknown):T\n}\n\nexport interface ConverseOptions<T> {\n    tools:readonly Tool[]\n    finalTool:string\n    final:FinalSpec<T>\n    maxTurns?:number\n    onTurn?:(info:TurnInfo) => void\n    inputByteCeiling?:number\n    workDeadline?:number      // ms since epoch\n    wrapUpWindow?:number      // ms\n    onWorkDeadline?:() => void\n    onBudgetExhausted?:() => void\n}\n\nexport interface Usage {\n    uncached_input_tokens:number\n    cached_input_tokens:number\n    cache_write_tokens:number\n    output_tokens:number\n    calls:number\n}\n\nexport interface Client {\n    readonly name:string  // request model name\n    converse<T>(system:string, user:string, opts:ConverseOptions<T>,\n        signal:AbortSignal):Promise<T>\n    completeStructured<T>(system:string, user:string, schemaName:string,\n        result:{schema:JsonSchemaObject, decode:FinalSpec<T>['decode']},\n        signal:AbortSignal):Promise<T>\n    usage():Usage\n}\n```\n\n`Usage` keeps snake_case keys because it is serialized into run records\nas is.\n\n### 3.4 Modules\n\n- `src/llm/errors.ts`\n  ```ts\n  export type Sentinel = 'no-final-call'|'work-deadline'|\n      'budget-exhausted'|'auth'|'endpoint'\n  export interface ErrorDetails {\n      model?:string\n      finishReason?:FinishCategory\n      rawFinishReason?:string\n      submissionAttempts?:number\n      recordRounds?:number\n      stopCause?:StopCauseKind\n  }\n  export class LlmError extends Error {\n      readonly sentinels:ReadonlySet<Sentinel>\n      readonly details:ErrorDetails\n  }\n  export function hasSentinel(err:unknown, s:Sentinel):boolean\n  export function cutoffError(cutoff:Sentinel|null, what:string,\n      cause?:unknown):LlmError\n  export function normalizeProviderError(callerSignal:AbortSignal,\n      model:string, err:unknown):unknown\n  export class CaptureError extends Error {}\n  ```\n  `hasSentinel` walks `sentinels` and the `cause` chain (so an endpoint\n  error wrapping a timeout still exposes the timeout via `cause`).\n  `cutoffError` must not put the cause in the matchable chain (2.14):\n  store it as `details`-only text, not as `cause`. `details` lets tests\n  assert the stop reason, counts, and finish reason without matching\n  message text. This module is shared with the protocols area, which\n  raises `auth` / `endpoint` errors.\n\n- `src/llm/ledger.ts`\n  ```ts\n  export const EST_BYTES_PER_TOKEN = 3\n  export const DEFAULT_FINAL_ALLOWANCE = 100_000\n  export const CACHED_TOKEN_WEIGHT = 0.1\n  export type Release = (usage:Usage) => void\n  export class Ledger {\n      reserve(reqBytes:number, maxOutput:number,\n          final:boolean):Release|null   // null = refused\n      exhausted():boolean\n      committed():{spent:number, limit:number}\n570:| sentinel | message |\n583:**Cutoff error** `cutoffError(what, cause?)`: matches the cutoff sentinel\n585:`<cutoff sentinel message>; <what>: <no-final-call message>` followed by\n590:generic sentinel, and the `no-final-call` text appears exactly once.\n655:(`review.ts`, `ledger.ts` math, `errors.ts`), so most invariants are unit\n789:- `src/llm/errors.ts`\n802:      readonly sentinels:ReadonlySet<Sentinel>\n812:  `hasSentinel` walks `sentinels` and the `cause` chain (so an endpoint\n964:  sentinels. The verify stage reads `ledger.exhausted()` before launching\n1008:Assertions use sentinels (`hasSentinel`), `LlmError.details`, call\n1026:  call, error matches the cutoff sentinel and `no-final-call`\n1134:  provider's error after a single generic sentinel\n1136:  (finish reason, attempts, model) plus the sentinel set.\n1165:- `internal/llm/errors.go` -- sentinels.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e41e09b0-fa4c-45a2-9b40-31ad5830b305","uuid":"cf6c4b42-c2d8-43c1-bc34-0b16e796297f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:44:33.736Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 3.7 Test fixtures\n\n- `test/helpers/env.ts`: `cleanEnv(base)` returns a copy of an env with\n  every variable whose upper-cased name starts with `ANTHROPIC_`,\n  `OPENAI_`, `OPENROUTER_`, or `ROAST_` removed. Tests build `io.env`\n  from it (plus `PATH`, `HOME` isolation, and explicit variables); no\n  test mutates `process.env`.\n- `test/helpers/inference-stream.ts`: `writeInferenceStream(res,\n  protocol, response)` turns a complete response object into the native\n  SSE stream for `anthropic`, `responses`, or `chat`, exactly as in\n  section 3.8. `writeJSONStream(res, protocol, body)` parses