{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAz8q5QL1GpGc6H3KePW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Construction fails for a blank or whitespace key, a non-positive max output tokens, and an unknown protocol, in the spec's order (A).\n[x] A `chat` request posts to the configured endpoint once, with only Roast's headers (credential, `User-Agent` `roast/<version>`, session headers), whatever provider, auth-token, or custom-header variables are set in the environment (A).\n[x] Reasoning-model IDs get `max_completion_tokens`, others `max_tokens`; forced tool choice is never sent (U on the encoder).\n[x] Tool schemas reach the request with `additionalProperties` and nested `required` lists intact (U on the encoder).\n[x] `requestBytes(request)` equals the byte length of the body actually sent (A).\n[x] A 3xx response is not followed, the redirect target receives no request and no key, and the error is an `EndpointError` that is not retryable (A).\n[x] An error body larger than 32 KiB is read only up to 32768 bytes (A).\n[x] Two concurrent conversations get distinct `roast-` session IDs, mirrored into the configured session header; each header is set once, and an environment naming that header does not change its value (A).\n[x] A capture-callback failure surfaces as `CaptureError` on that call and on every later call of the client, after exactly one HTTP request (A).\n[x] `Content-Length: 16777217` fails with the size error; an invalid JSON 2xx body fails once; streaming capture without `Content-Length` fails on overflow without calling the callback and never buffers more than the cap (A and U).\n[x] Streaming capture does not read ahead of the parser, preserves exactly the bytes read, and releases the body once (A with a controlled `ReadableStream`).\n[x] A request timeout yields an `EndpointError` whose cause is a timeout, within one second of the timeout (A).\n[x] Classification table: 408, 409, 429, 5xx, and `x-should-retry` retryable; 401, 403, 3xx, 400 not; transient stream types, incomplete streams, and transport errors retryable; aborts and `CaptureError` not (U).\n[x] `retryDelayMs` honors `retry-after-ms`, `retry-after` seconds, and `retry-after` dates, and ignores out-of-range hints (U).\n[x] `chat` usage `prompt_tokens: 100, cached_tokens: 30` normalizes to uncached 70 and cached 30, and cached 80 to 20 and 80; a chunk without usage after one with usage keeps the earlier usage (U).\n[x] Finish reasons `insufficient_system_resource`, `content_filter`, and an unknown value map to `error`, `content-filter`, and `unknown` with the raw reason exposed (U on the decoder).\n[x] The SSE parser handles CRLF, CR, and LF, multi-line data, comments, a missing final blank line, chunk boundaries inside a line and inside a UTF-8 sequence, and reads no further than the requested event (U).\n[x] `encodeToolResult` sorts keys and leaves `<`, `>`, `&`, and U+2028 unescaped; a lone surrogate in model output decodes to U+FFFD (U).\n[x] `hasSentinel` reports `auth` for an `AuthError` and `endpoint` for an `EndpointError`, including through a `cause` chain (U).\n[x] `writeInferenceStream` for `chat` emits the three chunks plus `[DONE]` of spec 01 section 3.8, and the `chat` decoder turns that stream back into the original tool calls, finish reason, and usage (U).\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nTicket 13 is finished and every checklist item passes: lint, typecheck, `npm run test:ts` (1207 passing) and `npm test` (all Go packages plus 22 launcher tests). It's in 8 commits on the branch. The notes file `.redeye/notes.md` is not committed.\n\n**What was built** (all in `src/llm/`):\n- **Pure modules:** `sse.ts`, `json.ts`, `types.ts`, `errors.ts`, `usage.ts`, `models.ts`, and `chat.ts` (the encoder and decoder).\n- **Modules that do I/O:** `http.ts`, `capture.ts`, `session.ts`, and `client.ts`.\n- **Test helpers:** `test/helpers/inference-stream.ts` (only the `chat` format for now) and a fake `node:http` server in `test/helpers/inference-server.ts`.\n\n`createModelClient` with `responses` or `anthropic` fails construction with the \"unsupported inference protocol\" error. Tickets 27 and 28 enable them by adding an entry to `ADAPTERS` in `client.ts`.\n\n**Decisions worth knowing:**\n- **Request timeout:** spec 2.12 puts the timeout in the agent loop, but the checklist tests it at `send()`. So `send` also applies `requestTimeoutMs`, and when it fires the error is an `EndpointError` caused by a `TimeoutError`. If ticket 14 adds its own timeout, whichever fires first wins, and a caller's abort reason is still rethrown unchanged.\n- **Error kinds:** I kept ticket 04's `kind` values (underscore names), which `src/cli/errors.ts` still reads, and added spec 07's hyphenated `sentinels`. The two must stay in step.\n- **Redirects:** a 3xx becomes an `EndpointError` that wraps the HTTP error. Other non-2xx responses throw the HTTP error directly, and `normalizeProviderError` turns 401 and 403 into `AuthError`.\n- **Byte-level tests:** the error-body cap, read-ahead and cancel counts are tested through `ClientConfig.fetch` with a controlled `ReadableStream`, because a real socket can't show how many bytes the client pulled.\n- **Ambient environment:** that test sets junk values in `process.env` and restores them afterwards.\n\n**TDD caveat:** I wrote `client.ts` and `capture.ts` before running their tests. To check the tests can actually fail, I broke the code on purpose in seven ways: following redirects, removing the capture gate check, removing the error-body cap, dropping the session header, skipping the body cancel, removing the timeout mapping, and calling the capture callback after an overflow. Every one made at least one test fail.\n\n**Gotcha:** the Write tool turned `\\uXXXX` escapes into literal characters in six files. I re-escaped them and confirmed `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` finds nothing. I also added an LLM-layer section to AGENTS.md covering module conventions and the test helpers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":361,"cache_read_input_tokens":188628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":361},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e41e09b0-fa4c-45a2-9b40-31ad5830b305","uuid":"bf1b62d2-7ad8-43f3-86b2-776ca3947932","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:59:14.127Z","request_id":"req_011ChAz8poYErC1Pcii58ajW"}
